{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550292397,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d388577f001jKAH9tjQFcF2el","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d3884627001F7q0JXxiefBacA","type":"tool","id":"call_81a6b7fb017d4f33a75ec15f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-218\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.0.13\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: [Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n40: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n41: - [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n42: - [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n43: - [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n44: - [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n45: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: [What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n55: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n60: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n61: [None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n62: \n63: | Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n64: |-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n65: | [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n66: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n72: - **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n73: - **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n74: - **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n75: - **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n76: \n77: [Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n78: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n84: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n89: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n90: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n95: [Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n96: \n97: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n98: - What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n99: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n100: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n101: \n102: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n103: - What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n104: - Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n109: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n110: - Completed pivots: 0\n111: - Failed pivots: 0\n112: - Audited overrides: 0\n113: - Swept: none yet\n114: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n115: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n116: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n121: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n122: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration. Includes target dimension and/or specific files to review.]\n129: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n134: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n135: \n136: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n137: \n138: Populate during initialization before the first review dimension runs. Keep this pointer-based and scoped to the declared review target:\n139: \n140: - Target pointers: files, specs, symbols, or resource-map entries under review.\n141: - Behavior claims: acceptance criteria, public contracts, or docs to verify.\n142: - Reuse and conventions: existing patterns that define expected implementation shape.\n143: - Review risks and gaps: stale graph or memory caveats, missing files, and out-of-scope areas.\n144: \n145: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use this snapshot only to seed review dimensions and final traceability.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n150: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n151: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n152: \n153: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n154: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n155: | `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n156: | `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n157: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n158: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n159: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n160: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n161: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n166: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n167: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n168: \n169: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n170: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n171: | [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n172: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n173: \n174: ---\n175: \n176: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n177: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n178: - Max iterations: [from config]\n179: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n180: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n181: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n182: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n183: - Session lineage: sessionId=[from config.sessionId], parentSessionId=[from config.parentSessionId], generation=[from config.generation], lineageMode=[from config.lineageMode]\n184: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n185: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n186: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n187: - Severity threshold: [from config.severityThreshold]\n188: - Review target type: [from config.reviewTargetType]\n189: - Cross-reference checks: core=[from config.crossReference.core], overlay=[from config.crossReference.overlay]\n190: - Started: [timestamp]\n191: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 17. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n196: \n197: Reference snippet showing a partially populated strategy file mid-review. Use this as a visual anchor when opening a live strategy doc.\n198: \n199: ```markdown\n200: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n201: - Target: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill, v1.4.0)\n202: - Dimensions: correctness, test-coverage, cross-runtime-parity, observability\n203: - Stop conditions: rolling newInfoRatio < 0.08 for 2 iterations OR all dimensions converged OR max=7 reached\n204: - Success criteria: zero P0 in correctness; test-coverage P0 resolved or deferred with rationale\n205: \n206: ## 4. NEXT FOCUS\n207: - Dimension: test-coverage\n208: - Files: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n209: - Why: Iteration 2 surfaced a P0 (convergence-path coverage gap); needs a focused follow-up before correctness can terminate PASS.\n210: \n211: ## 9. COVERAGE MATRIX\n212: | Dimension            | Status     | Iterations touched |\n213: |----------------------|------------|--------------------|\n214: | correctness          | converged  | 1                  |\n215: | test-coverage        | converging | 2, 4               |\n216: | cross-runtime-parity | converging | 3                  |\n217: | observability        | converging | 4                  |\n218: ```","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-218\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.0.13\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: [Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n40: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n41: - [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n42: - [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n43: - [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n44: - [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n45: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: [What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n55: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n60: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n61: [None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n62: \n63: | Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n64: |-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n65: | [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n66: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n72: - **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n73: - **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n74: - **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n75: - **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n76: \n77: [Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n78: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n84: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n89: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n90: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n95: [Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n96: \n97: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n98: - What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n99: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n100: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n101: \n102: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n103: - What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n104: - Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n109: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n110: - Completed pivots: 0\n111: - Failed pivots: 0\n112: - Audited overrides: 0\n113: - Swept: none yet\n114: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n115: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n116: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n121: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n122: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration. Includes target dimension and/or specific files to review.]\n129: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n134: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n135: \n136: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n137: \n138: Populate during initialization before the first review dimension runs. Keep this pointer-based and scoped to the declared review target:\n139: \n140: - Target pointers: files, specs, symbols, or resource-map entries under review.\n141: - Behavior claims: acceptance criteria, public contracts, or docs to verify.\n142: - Reuse and conventions: existing patterns that define expected implementation shape.\n143: - Review risks and gaps: stale graph or memory caveats, missing files, and out-of-scope areas.\n144: \n145: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use this snapshot only to seed review dimensions and final traceability.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n150: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n151: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n152: \n153: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n154: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n155: | `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n156: | `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n157: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n158: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n159: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n160: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n161: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n166: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n167: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n168: \n169: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n170: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n171: | [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n172: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n173: \n174: ---\n175: \n176: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n177: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n178: - Max iterations: [from config]\n179: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n180: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n181: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n182: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n183: - Session lineage: sessionId=[from config.sessionId], parentSessionId=[from config.parentSessionId], generation=[from config.generation], lineageMode=[from config.lineageMode]\n184: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n185: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n186: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n187: - Severity threshold: [from config.severityThreshold]\n188: - Review target type: [from config.reviewTargetType]\n189: - Cross-reference checks: core=[from config.crossReference.core], overlay=[from config.crossReference.overlay]\n190: - Started: [timestamp]\n191: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 17. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n196: \n197: Reference snippet showing a partially populated strategy file mid-review. Use this as a visual anchor when opening a live strategy doc.\n198: \n199: ```markdown\n200: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n201: - Target: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill, v1.4.0)\n202: - Dimensions: correctness, test-coverage, cross-runtime-parity, observability\n203: - Stop conditions: rolling newInfoRatio < 0.08 for 2 iterations OR all dimensions converged OR max=7 reached\n204: - Success criteria: zero P0 in correctness; test-coverage P0 resolved or deferred with rationale\n205: \n206: ## 4. NEXT FOCUS\n207: - Dimension: test-coverage\n208: - Files: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n209: - Why: Iteration 2 surfaced a P0 (convergence-path coverage gap); needs a focused follow-up before correctness can terminate PASS.\n210: \n211: ## 9. COVERAGE MATRIX\n212: | Dimension            | Status     | Iterations touched |\n213: |----------------------|------------|--------------------|\n214: | correctness          | converged  | 1                  |\n215: | test-coverage        | converging | 2, 4               |\n216: | cross-runtime-parity | converging | 3                  |\n217: | observability        | converging | 4                  |\n218: ```"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550290303,"end":1794550292397}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550292409,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38859cc001H04CGoeK5lkFxP","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d3884627001F7q0JXxiefBacA","type":"tool","id":"call_0f098a5921b8464cae3460db","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && awk '/phase_synthesis:/,0' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml | sed -n '1,260p'"},"output":"  phase_synthesis:\n    purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n    steps:\n\n      step_fanout_merge:\n        description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n        command: |\n          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n            --loop-type review \\\n            --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        wait_for_completion: true\n        bind_from_output:\n          p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n          p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n          p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n\n      step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n        action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        read_patterns:\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n        extract:\n          - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n          - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n          - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n          - p0_count: \"Total P0 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p1_count: \"Total P1 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p2_count: \"Total P2 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n          - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n          - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n          - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n\n      # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n      # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n      # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 findings (no P0)\n      # - FAIL: any P0 findings\n      # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n      step_derive_verdict:\n        action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if p0_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"FAIL\"\n          elif p1_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"CONDITIONAL\"\n          else:\n            verdict = \"PASS\"\n          has_advisories = (verdict == \"PASS\" and p2_count > 0)\n          ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\n        outputs:\n          - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n          - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n        contract: |\n          Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n          Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n\n      step_read_all_iterations:\n        action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n        read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n        read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_build_finding_registry:\n        action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n          2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n             content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n             Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n          3. Two-tier dedup:\n             PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n               - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n             FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n               - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n          4. Track finding lifecycle:\n             - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n             - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n             - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n          5. Resolve contradictions:\n             - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n             - Determine final severity and status\n          6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n        outputs:\n          - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n          - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n          - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n          - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n\n      step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n        action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          For each active P0/P1 finding:\n            1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n            2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n            3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n          Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n\n      step_emit_resource_map:\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n        action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n        write:\n          - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n        guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n        note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n\n      step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n        action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n        note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n\n      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        instructions: |\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state `hasSearchDebt: true` and carry the dashboard verdict as CONDITIONAL unless active P0 findings make it FAIL.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n\n      step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n        action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if active_p0 > 0:\n            release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n          elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n            release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n          else:\n            release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n        outputs:\n          - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n        note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n\n      step_convergence_report:\n        action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n          CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n          node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n            --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n            --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n            --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n            --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n            --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n            --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n            --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n            --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n            --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n            --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n          NODE_STATUS=$?\n          for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n            [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n            node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n            GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n            if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n              rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n              exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n            fi\n          done\n          rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n          exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n        note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n\n      step_update_config_status:\n        action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n        set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n\n      step_stage_artifact_dir:\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n        action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n        command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n        note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n        on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  # PHASE 4: SAVE\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  phase_save:\n    purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n    steps:\n\n      step_compose_save_payload:\n        action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n        output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n        requirements:\n          - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n          - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop.\"\n          - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n        example_payload: |\n          {\n            \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n            \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  phase_synthesis:\n    purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n    steps:\n\n      step_fanout_merge:\n        description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n        command: |\n          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n            --loop-type review \\\n            --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        wait_for_completion: true\n        bind_from_output:\n          p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n          p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n          p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n\n      step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n        action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        read_patterns:\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n        extract:\n          - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n          - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n          - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n          - p0_count: \"Total P0 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p1_count: \"Total P1 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p2_count: \"Total P2 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n          - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n          - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n          - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n\n      # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n      # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n      # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 findings (no P0)\n      # - FAIL: any P0 findings\n      # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n      step_derive_verdict:\n        action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if p0_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"FAIL\"\n          elif p1_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"CONDITIONAL\"\n          else:\n            verdict = \"PASS\"\n          has_advisories = (verdict == \"PASS\" and p2_count > 0)\n          ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\n        outputs:\n          - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n          - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n        contract: |\n          Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n          Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n\n      step_read_all_iterations:\n        action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n        read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n        read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_build_finding_registry:\n        action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n          2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n             content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n             Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n          3. Two-tier dedup:\n             PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n               - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n             FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n               - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n          4. Track finding lifecycle:\n             - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n             - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n             - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n          5. Resolve contradictions:\n             - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n             - Determine final severity and status\n          6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n        outputs:\n          - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n          - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n          - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n          - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n\n      step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n        action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          For each active P0/P1 finding:\n            1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n            2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n            3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n          Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n\n      step_emit_resource_map:\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n        action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n        write:\n          - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n        guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n        note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n\n      step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n        action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n        note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n\n      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        instructions: |\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state `hasSearchDebt: true` and carry the dashboard verdict as CONDITIONAL unless active P0 findings make it FAIL.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n\n      step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n        action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if active_p0 > 0:\n            release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n          elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n            release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n          else:\n            release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n        outputs:\n          - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n        note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n\n      step_convergence_report:\n        action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n          CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n          node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n            --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n            --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n            --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n            --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n            --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n            --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n            --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n            --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n            --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n            --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n          NODE_STATUS=$?\n          for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n            [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n            node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n            GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n            if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n              rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n              exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n            fi\n          done\n          rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n          exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n        note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n\n      step_update_config_status:\n        action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n        set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n\n      step_stage_artifact_dir:\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n        action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n        command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n        note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n        on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  # PHASE 4: SAVE\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  phase_save:\n    purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n    steps:\n\n      step_compose_save_payload:\n        action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n        output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n        requirements:\n          - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n          - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop.\"\n          - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n        example_payload: |\n          {\n            \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n            \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && awk '/phase_synthesis:/,0' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml | sed -n '1,260p'\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550290892,"end":1794550292409}}}}
