{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550412183,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d389c17e001vPPtxTcCmGwrWx","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d389aaa6001zEVDpK3R3kbR2X","type":"tool","id":"call_b6e9a06b3d3244f5ba7ea838","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - render-hooks-plugin lineage\ndescription: Session tracking for the render-hooks-plugin fan-out lineage of the command-surfacing review.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the `render-hooks-plugin` fan-out lineage. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Read by the executor at every iteration.\n- Updated in place after each iteration; machine-owned blocks stay inside their markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview of command surfacing for the `render-hooks-plugin` area of\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\nScope files are the `render-hooks-plugin` rows of `review/review-scope.txt` (53 files),\nplus shared docs that describe them (`.skilled/agents/orchestrate.md`,\n`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/*`, `system-skill-advisor` root docs).\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [x] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [x] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Implementing or editing any reviewed file. The review is observation-only.\n- Re-tuning the advisor scorer, embedders or the command corpus.\n- Reading or reproducing holdout prompt text. Counts only.\n- Reviewing areas owned by the sibling lineages (`scorer-attach`, `accuracy-runner`, `doctor-install`) beyond the shared docs that describe this area's surfaces.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence threshold 0.1 on the weighted new-findings ratio, minimum 2 iterations, stop policy `convergence`.\n- Hard ceiling `maxIterations = 5`.\n- A P0 that would need immediate operator action ends the loop early with `FAIL` and an escalation note.\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| D1 Correctness | CONDITIONAL | 1 | Session readers, hook fallback and render paths reviewed; two P1 findings on reader fan-out and fallback budget. |\n| D2 Security | CONDITIONAL | 2 | Plugin, session-reader transcript parsing and command-offer guidance reviewed; one P1 on injected-text containment in `dsh`. |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 3 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 5 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +1 P1, +1 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading each session reader against its own test file exposed contract drift faster than reading the reader alone (iteration 1).\n- Following the hook fallback path from `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` into `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` found the degraded-mode contract in one pass (iteration 1).\n- Mapping the review focus's runtime list (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh) onto concrete reader files first prevented a generic \"cross-runtime\" finding (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Treating `.d.mts` declaration files as independent evidence: they mirror `.mjs` signatures, so a drift there is only actionable when the `.mjs` disagrees (iteration 1).\n- Assuming the plugin README describes runtime coverage; it lists hooks, not per-runtime readers (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n### Declaration-file signature parity -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 2 attempts)\n- What was tried: comparing `.d.mts` bodies to `.mjs` implementations for behaviour claims.\n- Why blocked: the declarations carry types only, so every comparison resolved to \"consistent by construction\".\n- Do NOT retry: do not raise findings from `.d.mts`/`.d.mts.map` content alone.\n\n### Plugin README runtime matrix -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempt)\n- What was tried: deriving per-runtime behaviour claims from `.opencode/plugins/README.md`.\n- Why blocked: the README documents the plugin entry point only, never a runtime matrix.\n- Do NOT retry: derive runtime claims from `session-readers/*.mjs` and the feature catalog.\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 1\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: D1 Correctness (iteration 1), D2 Security (iteration 2)\n- Pivot lineage: 1 -> 2 (correctness -> security)\n- Remaining frontier: D3 traceability, D4 maintainability, cross-reference adjudication\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- \"Session readers re-read the whole transcript on every hook call\": ruled out; readers take a bounded tail window (iteration 1, evidence: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs`).\n- \"The plugin constructs a subprocess per prompt without a guard\": ruled out; the fallback path is budgeted and short-circuits (iteration 2, evidence: `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`).\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: docs-versus-code drift for the reviewed surfaces — `feature-catalog/cli-surface/*.md`, `feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`, `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `hooks/lib/README.md`, `.opencode/plugins/README.md`, and the `runtime-mirrors` README.\n- Reason: D1 and D2 raised three P1 findings whose fixes will change documented behaviour; the docs must be checked before the P1 set freezes.\n- Rotation status: D1 complete, D2 complete, D3 next, D4 after.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: `.d.mts` parity stays blocked; reader-vs-test comparison stays productive.\n- Required evidence: `file:line` on both sides of every doc claim, plus a named test or code path that contradicts it.\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: the 53 `render-hooks-plugin` rows of `review/review-scope.txt`. The area is the hook/plugin rendering surface: `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/*` (`claude`, `devin`, `dsh`, `pi`, `index`), the advisor runtime render/embedder/subprocess modules, the advisor CLI, and the runtime-mirror sync scripts.\n- Behaviour claims to verify: the advise hook must offer at most one command and must never auto-run a mutating command; each runtime reader must be isolated so one runtime's transcript cannot inject text into another's brief; holdout rows are never read by tune/fix/report paths.\n- Reuse and conventions: `sk-code` review doctrine; `system-deep-loop` deep-review packet; the sibling lineages own scorer, accuracy-runner and doctor-install surfaces.\n- Review risks and gaps: no `resource-map.md` at init, so the coverage gate is skipped; `codex` has no session reader in this area, so its behaviour is evidenced through the plugin/CLI path only.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | 1 | Spec docs describe the offer contract; code paths for two runtimes not yet exercised. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | No checklist evidence read yet. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | Pending iteration 3. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | Pending iteration 3. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | Pending iteration 3. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No manual-testing playbook row in this area. |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | D1, D2 | 2 | 0 P0, 1 P1, 1 P2 | partial |\n| `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/` (`claude`, `devin`, `dsh`, `pi`, `index`) | D1, D2 | 2 | 0 P0, 2 P1, 2 P2 | partial |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | D1, D2 | 2 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 1 P2 | partial |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | D1 | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 1 P2 | partial |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts` | D2 | 2 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n| remaining 48 scope files | - | - | - | pending |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-render-hooks-plugin-1794550137809-1ecgc7, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-13T06:12:00.000Z\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - render-hooks-plugin lineage\\ndescription: Session tracking for the render-hooks-plugin fan-out lineage of the command-surfacing review.\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the `render-hooks-plugin` fan-out lineage. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- Read by the executor at every iteration.\\n- Updated in place after each iteration; machine-owned blocks stay inside their markers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview of command surfacing for the `render-hooks-plugin` area of\\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\\nScope files are the `render-hooks-plugin` rows of `review/review-scope.txt` (53 files),\\nplus shared docs that describe them (`.skilled/agents/orchestrate.md`,\\n`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/*`, `system-skill-advisor` root docs).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\