{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550734937,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38e82b00014vGh4VJj7yTrWJ","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d38d7657001eeFOKLoyld1FZT","type":"tool","id":"call_7cee1f3c27df488c9918127f","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin`)\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — the `render-hooks-plugin` rows of `review/review-scope.txt`, plus shared docs that describe them\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: \"behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh\", read through the correctness lens — the six named runtimes resolve to the shared session-reader dispatcher plus the OpenCode hook/plugin entry point, which is what this pass executed line by line.\n- Budget profile: `verify` (12 analysis actions)\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1-80` — constants, imports, cache and concurrency bounds\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1086-1250` — per-instance state, run-slot acquisition, CLI invocation\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1440-1660` — `appendAdvisorBrief`, prompt recovery, fallback delivery\n- `.opencode/plugins/README.md:1-257` — documented plugin surface and env contract\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:1-147` — dispatcher, capability table, failure envelope\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:37-249` — store root, identity guard, loader\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:44-291` — project key, live branch, disk fallback\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:50-448` — SQLite projection, chain walk, transcript fallback\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:52-333` — Zstandard frame cutting, project key, event mapping\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:30-60`, `:188-262`, `:500-610` — command label, policy word, brief render\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:44-100` — policy and mutating vocabulary (read as consumer context)\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/injected-text.test.mjs:1-229` — injected-text contract across runtimes\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **Unknown runtime is reported as a missing locator, not a gated capability** -- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:99` -- `load()` validates the session id before it resolves the runtime, so `readSession({ runtime: 'cdoex', sessionId: '' })` returns `locator_unavailable`. A caller that typo'd the runtime name is told its locator is missing, and the `capability_gated` branch at `index.mjs:102` is unreachable for that shape.\nFinding class: instance-only\nScope proof: `index.mjs:97-105` is the only dispatch entry; both `readSession` (`:114`) and `loadSession` (`:133`) funnel through it, and neither pre-validates `runtime`, so the ordering at `:99` is the single decision point.\nAffected surface hints: [\"session-reader dispatcher\", \"history lookup callers\", \"capability table\"]\nCase: a caller passes a misspelled runtime and an empty session id; the envelope says the locator is unavailable and the runtime typo is never surfaced.\n\n2. **Containment is proven on the resolved path while the bytes are opened from the caller's path** -- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:213` -- `storePath = containment.path` is recorded as the source, but `claude.mjs:217` reads `transcriptPath`; the same split appears at `devin.mjs:350`/`:354` and `dsh.mjs:306`/`:310`. A file inside the store that is a link, or a path whose resolution changes between check and open, yields records whose `source.storePath` does not name the file that produced them.\nFinding class: cross-consumer\nScope proof: `rg -n \"storePath = containment.path\" .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers` returns exactly the three readers above; `pi.mjs:246-256` already closes the same gap by reading the guard's resolved path, and `opencode.mjs`/`codex.mjs` do not use a path locator, so the three sites are the whole class.\nAffected surface hints: [\"claude reader\", \"devin transcript fallback\", \"dsh reader\", \"history lookup\"]\nCase: a store file reachable through a link is accepted by containment and then re-opened by its link name, so the reported `storePath` can differ from the file actually read.\n\n3. **A DSH operator message with no `source` object is silently reclassified as injected** -- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195` -- a record is emitted only when `data.source?.kind === 'user'`, and `dsh.mjs:250` sends every other `user/message` to `injected`. An event that omits `source` therefore loses the operator's own turn from history while still reporting `ok: true`.\nFinding class: instance-only\nScope proof: `dsh.mjs:195-207` is the only user-record branch and `dsh.mjs:244-256` the only injected branch; `injected-text.test.mjs:174-206` exercises a non-operator source kind and an operator source kind, never an absent one, so no test pins the absent case.\nAffected surface hints: [\"dsh reader\", \"history lookup\", \"advisor brief prompt recovery\"]\nCase: a `user/message` event whose `data` has `role` and `content` but no `source` produces zero records and one injected entry.\n\n4. **A corrupt Devin `sessions.db` suppresses the transcript fallback** -- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:395` -- the database branch returns `store_unreadable` when `openDatabase` throws (`:403`), and a throw from `sessionRow` or the chain walk also returns `store_unreadable` (`:439`). Only an *absent* row or an *empty* projection falls through to `loadTranscript` at `:447`, so a store whose database is present but unreadable never reaches the JSON transcript that holds the same session.\nFinding class: class-of-bug\nScope proof: `devin.mjs:395-447` is the whole loader tail; the fallthrough at `:447` is reached only after the `if (row)` block at `:408` declines, and every `catch` on that path returns instead of falling through.\nAffected surface hints: [\"devin reader\", \"transcript fallback\", \"history lookup\"]\nCase: a Devin install whose `sessions.db` is truncated or locked returns `store_unreadable` although `transcripts/<sessionId>.json` on the same machine is intact.\n\n5. **`needsMode` withholding is defeated when the skill also has a generated command row** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:226` -- `commandLabel` resolves `recommendation.command ?? row?.command`, and the `(needs a mode)` head at `render.ts:550` is applied only when `commandRowFor(top.skill) === undefined`. A recommendation that withholds its command with `needsMode: true` therefore still prints a runnable command whenever its skill resolves a row, which is the outcome `render.ts:219-222` says the recommendation's own fields must prevent.\nFinding class: instance-only\nScope proof: `render.ts:226` is the only place `row?.command` backfills a recommendation, and `render.ts:550` is the only `needsMode` branch; `command-attach.ts:66-100` keys rows by `command-*` ids, so no hub skill that sets `needsMode` currently resolves one, which is the counterevidence that keeps this advisory.\nAffected surface hints: [\"brief renderer\", \"command label\", \"needsMode contract\"]\nCase: a recommendation with `needsMode: true`, no `command`, and a skill that has a generated row renders as `owner → /command (policy)` instead of `owner (needs a mode)`.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The offer contract in the reviewed renderer matches the typed-command policy vocabulary at `command-attach.ts:50-51` (`run`/`start`/`ask` × `read-only`/`add-only`/`mutates`). Two of the six named runtimes (`codex`, `opencode`) have no reader in this area's changed set, so their behaviour is evidenced only through the dispatcher contract. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | Deferred to the traceability dimension. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | Deferred. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | `index.mjs:28-65` declares seven runtimes; the six the operator named are all present, `cursor` is marked `gated`. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | Deferred to the traceability dimension. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No manual-testing playbook row covers this area. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:29-34` resolves every relative import against a real file: `lib/tool-identity.js`, `lib/v2-bridge.js`, `lib/opencode-message-identity.js`, `../hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs` and `../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/workspace/repo-root.mjs` all exist, so the plugin's load path is intact.\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:15-22` imports `codex`, `cursor`, `opencode`, `project` and `identity` readers that all exist beside it, so the dispatcher's import graph is complete.\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/injected-text.test.mjs` covers codex, pi, devin, dsh and opencode for injected-text containment; the claude attachment path is covered by `claude.test.mjs` (out of this iteration's read set).\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Runtime coverage gap (recorded, not a finding):** `codex` and `opencode` readers are unchanged files outside this area's diff, so the operator's \"behaviour on codex/opencode\" question is answered only through the shared dispatcher contract and the OpenCode plugin path. Named here so synthesis does not read this iteration as full six-runtime coverage.\n- **Declaration files:** `.d.mts` and `.d.mts.map` rows in scope carry types only. Comparing them to `.mjs` bodies produced no actionable difference, so they are recorded as consistent by construction rather than reviewed as behaviour.\n- **Absent `resource-map.md`:** the coverage gate is skipped for this packet, so no resource-map cross-check appears here.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `claude.mjs:196-198` refuses a subagent transcript before any read, so a side conversation cannot stand in for the parent session.\n- `claude.mjs:200-212` decides containment before opening the file, so an out-of-store path is refused without its content being read.\n- `pi.mjs:226-229` refuses `session_ambiguous` rather than guessing between two files that decode to one id.\n- `pi.mjs:242-244` uses the header `cwd` as the tie-breaker when separator flattening lets two projects share a directory name.\n- `dsh.mjs:286-293` resolves the session directory by exact id, so a newer decoy session is never opened.\n- `devin.mjs:111-131` refuses a chain with a cycle or a missing parent instead of emitting a partial conversation.\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1123-1124` bounds live advisor runs at `MAX_CONCURRENT_ADVISOR_RUNS = 2`, matching the README's \"Subprocess spawns ... are bounded\".\n- `render.ts:194-199` downgrades `start`, `ask` and any non-read-only `run` to parent-named for a child session, so a mutating command is not offered as startable to a dispatched child.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"Session readers re-read the whole transcript on every call\": ruled out. `claude.mjs:228-232` and `pi.mjs:261-266` parse a single file per call and `pi.mjs:56-65` probes only a bounded 64 KiB header prefix.\n- \"The plugin reads the prompt from the session on every turn\": ruled out. `system-skill-advisor.js:1473` fetches session messages only when `extractPrompt` returned nothing.\n- \"`decodeSessionLog` silently truncates a log\": ruled out. `dsh.mjs:52-80` throws on a truncated frame header or block, and `:94` throws on an unknown magic; only a 1-3 byte tail that cannot be a frame is skipped.\n- \"Declaration files disagree with their implementations\": ruled out as a review direction — the `.d.mts` bodies are type-only.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: the mutating-command offer path (`render.ts:194-258`, `command-attach.ts:66-110`) and the injected-text boundary in the four reviewed readers (`claude.mjs:174-183`, `dsh.mjs:244-256`, `devin.mjs:189-212`, `pi.mjs:165-174`).\n- Reason: correctness is clean of P0/P1, so the highest remaining risk in this area is a command the brief offers as startable and text one runtime's store can push into another runtime's history.\n- Rotation status: D1 complete, D2 next, then D3 traceability, D4 maintainability.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: `.d.mts` parity stays blocked; reader-vs-test comparison stays productive.\n- Required evidence: `file:line` on both the render decision and the policy row that supplies `mutating`, plus the exact store field that decides operator versus injected text.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 001\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin`)\\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — the `render-hooks-plugin` rows of `review/review-scope.txt`, plus shared docs that describe them\\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: \\\"behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh\\\", read through the correctness lens — the six named runtimes resolve to the shared session-reader dispatcher plus the OpenCode hook/plugin entry point, which is what this pass executed line by line.\\n- Budget profile: `verify` (12 analysis actions)\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1-80` — constants, imports, cache and concurrency bounds\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1086-1250` — per-instance state, run-slot acquisition, CLI invocation\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1440-1660` — `appendAdvisorBrief`, prompt recovery, fallback delivery\\n- `.opencode/plugins/README.md:1-257` — documented plugin surface and env contract\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:1-147` — dispatcher, capability table, failure envelope\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:37-249` — store root, identity guard, loader\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:44-291` — project key, live branch, disk fallback\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:50-448` — SQLite projection, chain walk, transcript fallback\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:52-333` — Zstandard frame cutting, project key, event mapping\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:30-60`, `:188-262`, `:500-610` — command label, policy word, brief render\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:44-100` — policy and mutating vocabulary (read as consumer context)\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/injected-text.test.mjs:1-229` — injected-text contract across runtimes\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **Unknown runtime is reported as a missing locator, not a gated capability** -- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:99` -- `load()` validates the session id before it resolves the runtime, so `readSession({ runtime: 'cdoex', sessionId: '' })` returns `locator_unavailable`. A caller that typo'd the runtime name is told its locator is missing, and the `capability_gated` branch at `index.mjs:102` is unreachable for that shape.\\nFinding class: instance-only\\nScope proof: `index.mjs:97-105` is the only dispatch entry; both `readSession` (`:114`) and `loadSession` (`:133`) funnel through it, and neither pre-validates `runtime`, so the ordering at `:99` is the single decision point.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"session-reader dispatcher\\\", \\\"history lookup callers\\\", \\\"capability table\\\"]\\nCase: a caller passes a misspelled runtime and an empty session id; the envelope says the locator is unavailable and the runtime typo is never surfaced.\\n\\n2. **Containment is proven on the resolved path while the bytes are opened from the caller's path** -- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:213` -- `storePath = containment.path` is recorded as the source, but `claude.mjs:217` reads `transcriptPath`; the same split appears at `devin.mjs:350`/`:354` and `dsh.mjs:306`/`:310`. A file inside the store that is a link, or a path whose resolution changes between check and open, yields records whose `source.storePath` does not name the file that produced them.\\nFinding class: cross-consumer\\nScope proof: `rg -n \\\"storePath = containment.path\\\" .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers` returns exactly the three readers above; `pi.mjs:246-256` already closes the same gap by reading the guard's resolved path, and `opencode.mjs`/`codex.mjs` do not use a path locator, so the three sites are the whole class.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"claude reader\\\", \\\"devin transcript fallback\\\", \\\"dsh reader\\\", \\\"history lookup\\\"]\\nCase: a store file reachable through a link is accepted by containment and then re-opened by its link name, so the reported `storePath` can differ from the file actually read.\\n\\n3. **A DSH operator message with no `source` object is silently reclassified as injected** -- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195` -- a record is emitted only when `data.source?.kind === 'user'`, and `dsh.mjs:250` sends every other `user/message` to `injected`. An event that omits `source` therefore loses the operator's own turn from history while still reporting `ok: true`.\\nFinding class: instance-only\\nScope proof: `dsh.mjs:195-207` is the only user-record branch and `dsh.mjs:244-256` the only injected branch; `injected-text.test.mjs:174-206` exercises a non-operator source kind and an operator source kind, never an absent one, so no test pins the absent case.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"dsh reader\\\", \\\"history lookup\\\", \\\"advisor brief prompt recovery\\\"]\\nCase: a `user/message` event whose `data` has `role` and `content` but no `source` produces zero records and one injected entry.\\n\\n4. **A corrupt Devin `sessions.db` suppresses the transcript fallback** -- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:395` -- the database branch returns `store_unreadable` when `openDatabase` throws (`:403`), and a throw from `sessionRow` or the chain walk also returns `store_unreadable` (`:439`). Only an *absent* row or an *empty* projection falls through to `loadTranscript` at `:447`, so a store whose database is present but unreadable never reaches the JSON transcript that holds the same session.\\nFinding class: class-of-bug\\nScope proof: `devin.mjs:395-447` is the whole loader tail; the fallthrough at `:447` is reached only after the `if (row)` block at `:408` declines, and every `catch` on that path returns instead of falling through.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"devin reader\\\", \\\"transcript fallback\\\", \\\"history lookup\\\"]\\nCase: a Devin install whose `sessions.db` is truncated or locked returns `store_unreadable` although `transcripts/<sessionId>.json` on the same machine is intact.\\n\\n5. **`needsMode` withholding is defeated when the skill also has a generated command row** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:226` -- `commandLabel` resolves `recommendation.command ?? row?.command`, and the `(needs a mode)` head at `render.ts:550` is applied only when `commandRowFor(top.skill) === undefined`. A recommendation that withholds its command with `needsMode: true` therefore still prints a runnable command whenever its skill resolves a row, which is the outcome `render.ts:219-222` says the recommendation's own fields must prevent.\\nFinding class: instance-only\\nScope proof: `render.ts:226` is the only place `row?.command` backfills a recommendation, and `render.ts:550` is the only `needsMode` branch; `command-attach.ts:66-100` keys rows by `command-*` ids, so no hub skill that sets `needsMode` currently resolves one, which is the counterevidence that keeps this advisory.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"brief renderer\\\", \\\"command label\\\", \\\"needsMode contract\\\"]\\nCase: a recommendation with `needsMode: true`, no `command`, and a skill that has a generated row renders as `owner → /command (policy)` instead of `owner (needs a mode)`.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The offer contract in the reviewed renderer matches the typed-command policy vocabulary at `command-attach.ts:50-51` (`run`/`start`/`ask` × `read-only`/`add-only`/`mutates`). Two of the six named runtimes (`codex`, `opencode`) have no reader in this area's changed set, so their behaviour is evidenced only through the dispatcher contract. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | Deferred to the traceability dimension. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | Deferred. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | `index.mjs:28-65` declares seven runtimes; the six the operator named are all present, `cursor` is marked `gated`. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | Deferred to the traceability dimension. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No manual-testing playbook row covers this area. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:29-34` resolves every relative import against a real file: `lib/tool-identity.js`, `lib/v2-bridge.js`, `lib/opencode-message-identity.js`, `../hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs` and `../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/workspace/repo-root.mjs` all exist, so the plugin's load path is intact.\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:15-22` imports `codex`, `cursor`, `opencode`, `project` and `identity` readers that all exist beside it, so the dispatcher's import graph is complete.\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/injected-text.test.mjs` covers codex, pi, devin, dsh and opencode for injected-text containment; the claude attachment path is covered by `claude.test.mjs` (out of this iteration's read set).\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Runtime coverage gap (recorded, not a finding):** `codex` and `opencode` readers are unchanged files outside this area's diff, so the operator's \\\"behaviour on codex/opencode\\\" question is answered only through the shared dispatcher contract and the OpenCode plugin path. Named here so synthesis does not read this iteration as full six-runtime coverage.\\n- **Declaration files:** `.d.mts` and `.d.mts.map` rows in scope carry types only. Comparing them to `.mjs` bodies produced no actionable difference, so they are recorded as consistent by construction rather than reviewed as behaviour.\\n- **Absent `resource-map.md`:** the coverage gate is skipped for this packet, so no resource-map cross-check appears here.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `claude.mjs:196-198` refuses a subagent transcript before any read, so a side conversation cannot stand in for the parent session.\\n- `claude.mjs:200-212` decides containment before opening the file, so an out-of-store path is refused without its content being read.\\n- `pi.mjs:226-229` refuses `session_ambiguous` rather than guessing between two files that decode to one id.\\n- `pi.mjs:242-244` uses the header `cwd` as the tie-breaker when separator flattening lets two projects share a directory name.\\n- `dsh.mjs:286-293` resolves the session directory by exact id, so a newer decoy session is never opened.\\n- `devin.mjs:111-131` refuses a chain with a cycle or a missing parent instead of emitting a partial conversation.\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1123-1124` bounds live advisor runs at `MAX_CONCURRENT_ADVISOR_RUNS = 2`, matching the README's \\\"Subprocess spawns ... are bounded\\\".\\n- `render.ts:194-199` downgrades `start`, `ask` and any non-read-only `run` to parent-named for a child session, so a mutating command is not offered as startable to a dispatched child.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"Session readers re-read the whole transcript on every call\\\": ruled out. `claude.mjs:228-232` and `pi.mjs:261-266` parse a single file per call and `pi.mjs:56-65` probes only a bounded 64 KiB header prefix.\\n- \\\"The plugin reads the prompt from the session on every turn\\\": ruled out. `system-skill-advisor.js:1473` fetches session messages only when `extractPrompt` returned nothing.\\n- \\\"`decodeSessionLog` silently truncates a log\\\": ruled out. `dsh.mjs:52-80` throws on a truncated frame header or block, and `:94` throws on an unknown magic; only a 1-3 byte tail that cannot be a frame is skipped.\\n- \\\"Declaration files disagree with their implementations\\\": ruled out as a review direction — the `.d.mts` bodies are type-only.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Focus area: the mutating-command offer path (`render.ts:194-258`, `command-attach.ts:66-110`) and the injected-text boundary in the four reviewed readers (`claude.mjs:174-183`, `dsh.mjs:244-256`, `devin.mjs:189-212`, `pi.mjs:165-174`).\\n- Reason: correctness is clean of P0/P1, so the highest remaining risk in this area is a command the brief offers as startable and text one runtime's store can push into another runtime's history.\\n- Rotation status: D1 complete, D2 next, then D3 traceability, D4 maintainability.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: `.d.mts` parity stays blocked; reader-vs-test comparison stays productive.\\n- Required evidence: `file:line` on both the render decision and the policy row that supplies `mutating`, plus the exact store field that decides operator versus injected text.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550694576,"end":1794550734937}}}}
