{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551010040,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d392acfd001fzhPHosHd3Q3uP","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d3926a1a00123vNNsFnvyix0e","type":"tool","id":"call_346b0fd843154ef1bbad6c7b","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin`)\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin`\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: \"safety of offering a mutating command\" and \"holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows\". Both were executed directly: the command-offer guard was traced from the policy vocabulary to the rendered label, and the advisor runtime, hook library, plugin and session readers were searched for any holdout read path.\n- Budget profile: `adjudicate` (9 analysis actions)\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:140-190`, `:188-262`, `:500-610` — label sanitizer, child downgrade, brief render\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:44-110` — policy and mutating vocabulary\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:180-260` — spawn, env, stdout accumulation\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts:60-100` — brief options surface\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:200-300` — child env, stdout cap, process-group kill\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:340-370`, `:470-510` — policy producer\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:255-300`, `:540-600`, `:1240-1280` — recommendations mapper, CLI spawn env\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:160-183`, `pi.mjs:162-174`, `devin.mjs:185-212`, `dsh.mjs:240-256` — injected-text boundary\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **The child-session command downgrade is decided only by a process-wide env flag** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:522` -- `const childSession = options.childSession ?? process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. The option exists on the renderer's own type (`render.ts:51`) but not on `SkillAdvisorBriefOptions` (`skill-advisor-brief.ts:75-82`, which carries `workspaceRoot`, `runtime`, `maxTokens`, `thresholdConfig` and `subprocessTimeoutMs` only), so no hook or plugin can classify a session per request. The OpenCode plugin then spawns the advisor CLI with the host's environment (`system-skill-advisor.js:1268`), and the hook fallback forwards that environment unchanged (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:206-212`). Every session a single host process serves therefore receives the same classification, and `parentNamedOnly` (`render.ts:194-199`) never fires for a child that the host dispatches in-process.\nFinding class: cross-consumer\nScope proof: `rg -n \"childSession\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .skilled/hooks .opencode/hooks` returns the renderer only; `skill-advisor-brief.ts` exposes no such option, `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:206-212` never sets or infers it, and `system-skill-advisor.js` never passes it. So the env flag at `render.ts:522` is the sole input on every production path.\nAffected surface hints: [\"brief renderer\", \"hook CLI fallback\", \"OpenCode advisor plugin\", \"child-session policy\"]\nCase: a host process that launched without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` dispatches an in-process subagent; that child's brief renders `/create:readme (start)` or `/deep:review (ask)` as fully visible instead of `(parent-named)`, so the child is invited to start a command the guard exists to withhold.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"claim\",\n  \"claim\": \"The child-session command downgrade depends on a process-wide environment flag that no caller can override per session, so a child rendered by a host process launched as a parent receives no downgrade.\",\n  \"evidenceRefs\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:522\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts:75\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:206\",\n    \".opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1268\"\n  ],\n  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Searched every caller of renderAdvisorBrief for an explicit childSession argument; found none outside the renderer's own type. Checked whether childEnvForCli sets AI_SESSION_CHILD per request; it sets SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR and SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_PROMPT_TIME only.\",\n  \"alternativeExplanation\": \"Each host may dispatch children as fresh processes started with AI_SESSION_CHILD=1, in which case the flag is correct for every child and the guard holds. The reviewed code cannot distinguish that deployment from an in-process one.\",\n  \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Proof that every host which renders a child brief launches a dedicated process with AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 set at spawn; that would make the env flag a faithful per-session signal and reduce this to P2 (missing per-session override).\"\n}\n```\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n2. **The low-level advisor spawn accumulates child output without a byte cap** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:239` -- `stdout += chunk` runs with no ceiling, while the hook fallback caps the same stream through `capStdout` against `MAX_STDOUT_BYTES` (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:214-219`). Only `timeoutMs` bounds the wait, so a child that keeps writing grows the caller's heap for the whole timeout.\nFinding class: cross-consumer\nScope proof: `subprocess.ts` defines no `MAX_*` constant and both `stdout +=` and the stderr listener append unbounded; the fallback path in the same skill caps both, so the two consumers of one CLI disagree on boundedness.\nAffected surface hints: [\"advisor subprocess\", \"hook CLI fallback\", \"advisor daemon\"]\nCase: a CLI that emits a long stream — a runaway log line or a large JSON envelope — grows the parent process memory without limit until the timeout kills it.\n\n3. **The child downgrade reads mutability from the skill row, not from the command that is printed** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:233` -- `policyWord(policy, row?.mutating, childSession)` takes `mutating` from `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)`, while the printed command may come from `recommendation.command` (`render.ts:226`). When a recommendation supplies its own command and the row for its skill describes a different one, the downgrade decision is made on the row's mutability rather than the command's.\nFinding class: instance-only\nScope proof: `render.ts:223-237` is the only label builder; `row?.mutating` is read exactly once at `:233`, and `advise` producers in `advisor-recommend.ts:356-359` and `:502-503` always pair a command with its own row, which is the counterevidence that keeps this advisory.\nAffected surface hints: [\"brief renderer\", \"command label\", \"child-session policy\"]\nCase: a recommendation from a caller that attaches `/doctor:overlay apply` while resolving the read-only `sk-doc` row renders `(run)` in a child because `row.mutating` says `read-only`.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The three-word policy vocabulary at `command-attach.ts:50` (`run`/`start`/`ask`) maps one-to-one onto `parentNamedOnly` at `render.ts:194-199`; no policy value escapes the downgrade except `run` with `read-only`. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | Deferred to the traceability dimension. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | Deferred. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | The downgrade is the same code on every runtime, which is exactly why finding 1 is cross-runtime rather than runtime-specific. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | Deferred. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook row covers this area. |\n\n## Holdout Hygiene Check\n\n- Searched `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts`, `hooks/`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` and `.skilled/hooks/shared` for `holdout`. The only hit is prose in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:94` (\"Corpus/holdout/parity/safety/latency slices still render\"), which is a validation note, not a read path.\n- No tune, fix, report or scoring path inside this area opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or the split holdout inside `command-prompts.jsonl`. Recorded as a confirmed-clean surface, not as a finding. No holdout row was read or printed by this iteration.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:356-359` and `:502-503` both take `policy` from the same generated row as `command`, so the renderer's `recommendation.policy ?? row?.policy` precedence (`render.ts:227`) does not currently diverge from the row.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:279-292` documents and implements a process-group kill for the shim's grandchild (`detached: true` plus `process.kill(-pid)`), so a timed-out advisor cannot outlive the hook budget.\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1123-1124` bounds concurrent advisor runs at 2, and `:1268` passes the inherited environment to each spawn.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Same-process vs per-process child dispatch (finding 1):** the reviewed code cannot tell these apart. The finding states the in-process case as its reach and records the per-process case as the downgrade trigger, rather than asserting which host does which.\n- **Declaration files:** not re-entered, per the exhausted-approach record.\n- **`cursor` runtime:** declared `gated` in the capability table (`index.mjs:59-64`) and has no reader in this area's changed set, so it is outside the operator's named six and was not reviewed as a security surface.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `render.ts:159-175` refuses a skill label that is multi-line or matches `INSTRUCTION_LABEL_PATTERN`, so a repository-authored label cannot place a second line into the brief.\n- `render.ts:194-199` downgrades every `start`, every `ask` and every non-read-only `run` to `PARENT_NAMED_POLICY` for a child, which is the intended containment shape; the defect in finding 1 is the input to this function, not the function.\n- `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:277-278` sends the user's prompt on stdin, never in argv, so it does not appear in the process table.\n- `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:214-219` caps the fallback path's stdout at `MAX_STDOUT_BYTES`.\n- `claude.mjs:174-183`, `pi.mjs:165-174`, `devin.mjs:189-212` and `dsh.mjs:244-256` all keep injected harness text out of `records`, so one runtime's stored hook brief cannot be re-read as operator text.\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1631-1657` wraps the whole delivery path so a failure injects a status-headed fallback and never blocks the prompt; no path writes to stdout or stderr.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"The plugin passes the raw CLI stdout into model context\": ruled out. `cliRecommendations` (`system-skill-advisor.js:558-591`) copies only `skillId`, numeric scores, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`, `needsMode` and `ambiguousWith`, each type-checked.\n- \"A recommendation can relabel a mutating command as `read-only` to escape the child downgrade\": ruled out. `command-attach.ts:50-51` is the only `mutating` vocabulary, `render.ts:233` reads it from the generated row, and the CLI response has no `mutating` field (verified against `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:228-245` and `advisor-recommend.ts:356-359`).\n- \"The hook fallback leaves an advisor grandchild running after a timeout\": ruled out. `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:279-292` kills the process group.\n- \"An env-secret value reaches the advisor through argv\": ruled out. The payload is written to stdin.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: docs-versus-code drift across `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/skill-advisor-cli.md`, `feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`, `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `hooks/lib/README.md`, `.opencode/plugins/README.md`, and `runtime-mirrors/README.md`, checked against the code this iteration and iteration 1 read.\n- Reason: three P1-relevant behaviours are now pinned (child downgrade input, fallback envelope, injected-text boundary); the documents that describe them must be checked before the finding set freezes.\n- Rotation status: D1 and D2 complete, D3 next, D4 after.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: `.d.mts` parity stays blocked; the `README`-vs-constant comparison (found `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` documented as 3000 against `DEFAULT_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500`) is productive and becomes concrete evidence this iteration.\n- Required evidence: `file:line` on both sides of every doc claim.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin`)\\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin`\\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: \\\"safety of offering a mutating command\\\" and \\\"holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows\\\". Both were executed directly: the command-offer guard was traced from the policy vocabulary to the rendered label, and the advisor runtime, hook library, plugin and session readers were searched for any holdout read path.\\n- Budget profile: `adjudicate` (9 analysis actions)\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:140-190`, `:188-262`, `:500-610` — label sanitizer, child downgrade, brief render\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:44-110` — policy and mutating vocabulary\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:180-260` — spawn, env, stdout accumulation\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts:60-100` — brief options surface\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:200-300` — child env, stdout cap, process-group kill\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:340-370`, `:470-510` — policy producer\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:255-300`, `:540-600`, `:1240-1280` — recommendations mapper, CLI spawn env\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:160-183`, `pi.mjs:162-174`, `devin.mjs:185-212`, `dsh.mjs:240-256` — injected-text boundary\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\n1. **The child-session command downgrade is decided only by a process-wide env flag** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:522` -- `const childSession = options.childSession ?? process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. The option exists on the renderer's own type (`render.ts:51`) but not on `SkillAdvisorBriefOptions` (`skill-advisor-brief.ts:75-82`, which carries `workspaceRoot`, `runtime`, `maxTokens`, `thresholdConfig` and `subprocessTimeoutMs` only), so no hook or plugin can classify a session per request. The OpenCode plugin then spawns the advisor CLI with the host's environment (`system-skill-advisor.js:1268`), and the hook fallback forwards that environment unchanged (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:206-212`). Every session a single host process serves therefore receives the same classification, and `parentNamedOnly` (`render.ts:194-199`) never fires for a child that the host dispatches in-process.\\nFinding class: cross-consumer\\nScope proof: `rg -n \\\"childSession\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .skilled/hooks .opencode/hooks` returns the renderer only; `skill-advisor-brief.ts` exposes no such option, `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:206-212` never sets or infers it, and `system-skill-advisor.js` never passes it. So the env flag at `render.ts:522` is the sole input on every production path.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"brief renderer\\\", \\\"hook CLI fallback\\\", \\\"OpenCode advisor plugin\\\", \\\"child-session policy\\\"]\\nCase: a host process that launched without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` dispatches an in-process subagent; that child's brief renders `/create:readme (start)` or `/deep:review (ask)` as fully visible instead of `(parent-named)`, so the child is invited to start a command the guard exists to withhold.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The child-session command downgrade depends on a process-wide environment flag that no caller can override per session, so a child rendered by a host process launched as a parent receives no downgrade.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidenceRefs\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:522\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts:75\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:206\\\",\\n    \\\".opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1268\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counterevidenceSought\\\": \\\"Searched every caller of renderAdvisorBrief for an explicit childSession argument; found none outside the renderer's own type. Checked whether childEnvForCli sets AI_SESSION_CHILD per request; it sets SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR and SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_PROMPT_TIME only.\\\",\\n  \\\"alternativeExplanation\\\": \\\"Each host may dispatch children as fresh processes started with AI_SESSION_CHILD=1, in which case the flag is correct for every child and the guard holds. The reviewed code cannot distinguish that deployment from an in-process one.\\\",\\n  \\\"finalSeverity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.6,\\n  \\\"downgradeTrigger\\\": \\\"Proof that every host which renders a child brief launches a dedicated process with AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 set at spawn; that would make the env flag a faithful per-session signal and reduce this to P2 (missing per-session override).\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n2. **The low-level advisor spawn accumulates child output without a byte cap** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:239` -- `stdout += chunk` runs with no ceiling, while the hook fallback caps the same stream through `capStdout` against `MAX_STDOUT_BYTES` (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:214-219`). Only `timeoutMs` bounds the wait, so a child that keeps writing grows the caller's heap for the whole timeout.\\nFinding class: cross-consumer\\nScope proof: `subprocess.ts` defines no `MAX_*` constant and both `stdout +=` and the stderr listener append unbounded; the fallback path in the same skill caps both, so the two consumers of one CLI disagree on boundedness.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"advisor subprocess\\\", \\\"hook CLI fallback\\\", \\\"advisor daemon\\\"]\\nCase: a CLI that emits a long stream — a runaway log line or a large JSON envelope — grows the parent process memory without limit until the timeout kills it.\\n\\n3. **The child downgrade reads mutability from the skill row, not from the command that is printed** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:233` -- `policyWord(policy, row?.mutating, childSession)` takes `mutating` from `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)`, while the printed command may come from `recommendation.command` (`render.ts:226`). When a recommendation supplies its own command and the row for its skill describes a different one, the downgrade decision is made on the row's mutability rather than the command's.\\nFinding class: instance-only\\nScope proof: `render.ts:223-237` is the only label builder; `row?.mutating` is read exactly once at `:233`, and `advise` producers in `advisor-recommend.ts:356-359` and `:502-503` always pair a command with its own row, which is the counterevidence that keeps this advisory.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"brief renderer\\\", \\\"command label\\\", \\\"child-session policy\\\"]\\nCase: a recommendation from a caller that attaches `/doctor:overlay apply` while resolving the read-only `sk-doc` row renders `(run)` in a child because `row.mutating` says `read-only`.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The three-word policy vocabulary at `command-attach.ts:50` (`run`/`start`/`ask`) maps one-to-one onto `parentNamedOnly` at `render.ts:194-199`; no policy value escapes the downgrade except `run` with `read-only`. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | Deferred to the traceability dimension. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | Deferred. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | The downgrade is the same code on every runtime, which is exactly why finding 1 is cross-runtime rather than runtime-specific. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | Deferred. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook row covers this area. |\\n\\n## Holdout Hygiene Check\\n\\n- Searched `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts`, `hooks/`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` and `.skilled/hooks/shared` for `holdout`. The only hit is prose in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:94` (\\\"Corpus/holdout/parity/safety/latency slices still render\\\"), which is a validation note, not a read path.\\n- No tune, fix, report or scoring path inside this area opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or the split holdout inside `command-prompts.jsonl`. Recorded as a confirmed-clean surface, not as a finding. No holdout row was read or printed by this iteration.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:356-359` and `:502-503` both take `policy` from the same generated row as `command`, so the renderer's `recommendation.policy ?? row?.policy` precedence (`render.ts:227`) does not currently diverge from the row.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:279-292` documents and implements a process-group kill for the shim's grandchild (`detached: true` plus `process.kill(-pid)`), so a timed-out advisor cannot outlive the hook budget.\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1123-1124` bounds concurrent advisor runs at 2, and `:1268` passes the inherited environment to each spawn.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Same-process vs per-process child dispatch (finding 1):** the reviewed code cannot tell these apart. The finding states the in-process case as its reach and records the per-process case as the downgrade trigger, rather than asserting which host does which.\\n- **Declaration files:** not re-entered, per the exhausted-approach record.\\n- **`cursor` runtime:** declared `gated` in the capability table (`index.mjs:59-64`) and has no reader in this area's changed set, so it is outside the operator's named six and was not reviewed as a security surface.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `render.ts:159-175` refuses a skill label that is multi-line or matches `INSTRUCTION_LABEL_PATTERN`, so a repository-authored label cannot place a second line into the brief.\\n- `render.ts:194-199` downgrades every `start`, every `ask` and every non-read-only `run` to `PARENT_NAMED_POLICY` for a child, which is the intended containment shape; the defect in finding 1 is the input to this function, not the function.\\n- `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:277-278` sends the user's prompt on stdin, never in argv, so it does not appear in the process table.\\n- `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:214-219` caps the fallback path's stdout at `MAX_STDOUT_BYTES`.\\n- `claude.mjs:174-183`, `pi.mjs:165-174`, `devin.mjs:189-212` and `dsh.mjs:244-256` all keep injected harness text out of `records`, so one runtime's stored hook brief cannot be re-read as operator text.\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1631-1657` wraps the whole delivery path so a failure injects a status-headed fallback and never blocks the prompt; no path writes to stdout or stderr.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"The plugin passes the raw CLI stdout into model context\\\": ruled out. `cliRecommendations` (`system-skill-advisor.js:558-591`) copies only `skillId`, numeric scores, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`, `needsMode` and `ambiguousWith`, each type-checked.\\n- \\\"A recommendation can relabel a mutating command as `read-only` to escape the child downgrade\\\": ruled out. `command-attach.ts:50-51` is the only `mutating` vocabulary, `render.ts:233` reads it from the generated row, and the CLI response has no `mutating` field (verified against `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:228-245` and `advisor-recommend.ts:356-359`).\\n- \\\"The hook fallback leaves an advisor grandchild running after a timeout\\\": ruled out. `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:279-292` kills the process group.\\n- \\\"An env-secret value reaches the advisor through argv\\\": ruled out. The payload is written to stdin.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Focus area: docs-versus-code drift across `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/skill-advisor-cli.md`, `feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`, `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `hooks/lib/README.md`, `.opencode/plugins/README.md`, and `runtime-mirrors/README.md`, checked against the code this iteration and iteration 1 read.\\n- Reason: three P1-relevant behaviours are now pinned (child downgrade input, fallback envelope, injected-text boundary); the documents that describe them must be checked before the finding set freezes.\\n- Rotation status: D1 and D2 complete, D3 next, D4 after.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: `.d.mts` parity stays blocked; the `README`-vs-constant comparison (found `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` documented as 3000 against `DEFAULT_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500`) is productive and becomes concrete evidence this iteration.\\n- Required evidence: `file:line` on both sides of every doc claim.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550967549,"end":1794551010040}}}}
