{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551092790,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39494fb001eOt26htewf6WG4","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d39476f2001foFvRVVChycgBF","type":"tool","id":"call_bb9c23de6b494163b9096f00","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && cat -n .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md"},"output":"     1\t---\n     2\ttitle: \"Shared: Session Readers\"\n     3\tdescription: \"The read-only session reader package: one exact-id reader per runtime, the shared failure envelope, the capability table and the projection to the HistoryEntry list.\"\n     4\ttrigger_phrases:\n     5\t  - \"session readers\"\n     6\t  - \"read session history\"\n     7\t  - \"session reader capabilities\"\n     8\t  - \"exact session id reader\"\n     9\tversion: 1.0.0.0\n    10\t---\n    11\t\n    12\t# Shared: Session Readers\n    13\t\n    14\t---\n    15\t\n    16\t## 1. OVERVIEW\n    17\t\n    18\tThis package reads one runtime session by its exact id and returns it as the shared `HistoryEntry` list that the history lookup core takes. It never writes. A reader opens a store read-only, proves the file or row belongs to the requested session, and returns a failure code rather than a partial list.\n    19\t\n    20\tThe six decision-capture sweeps keep their own inline readers and remain the writers. Nothing here changes a save-time path.\n    21\t\n    22\t---\n    23\t\n    24\t## 2. CONTRACT\n    25\t\n    26\t- **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n    27\t- **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n    28\t- **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n    29\t- **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n    30\t\n    31\t`loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\n    32\t\n    33\t- Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n    34\t- Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\n    35\t- Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\n    36\t- DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\n    37\t\n    38\tFailure codes:\n    39\t\n    40\t| Code | Meaning |\n    41\t|---|---|\n    42\t| `locator_unavailable` | The id is empty or unsafe, or the runtime has no locator to resolve |\n    43\t| `capability_gated` | No reader exists for the runtime, or its switch is off |\n    44\t| `session_not_found` | No store record matches the id |\n    45\t| `session_mismatch` | A record was found, but its recorded id or path does not match |\n    46\t| `session_ambiguous` | More than one record claims the id |\n    47\t| `store_unreadable` | The store could not be read or projected |\n    48\t\n    49\t---\n    50\t\n    51\t## 3. FILES\n    52\t\n    53\t| File | Role |\n    54\t|---|---|\n    55\t| `index.mjs` | The dispatcher: `readSession` (projected entries), `loadSession` (raw records), the `capabilities` table and the failure envelope |\n    56\t| `identity.mjs` | Shared guards: safe session ids, path containment and the recorded-id check |\n    57\t| `project.mjs` | Projection from neutral records to `HistoryEntry`, with tool-call pairing |\n    58\t| `claude.mjs` | Claude Code transcript reader |\n    59\t| `codex.mjs` | Codex session log reader |\n    60\t| `pi.mjs` | Pi session log reader, following the live branch |\n    61\t| `opencode.mjs` | OpenCode SQLite store reader, which proves the session's recorded directory when the caller names one |\n    62\t| `devin.mjs` | Devin `sessions.db` reader over the session's main message chain and, through each compaction's `summarized_from` link, the threads before it. A recorded folder at or below the named folder passes, because Devin's hooks receive the project root. Falls back to the transcript file for a store without the session's turns |\n    63\t| `dsh.mjs` | DSH session log reader |\n    64\t| `cursor.mjs` | Cursor gate, which returns before touching any file |\n    65\t\n    66\t---\n    67\t\n    68\t## 4. VALIDATION\n    69\t\n    70\tFrom the repository root:\n    71\t\n    72\t```bash\n    73\tnode --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/\n    74\t```\n    75\t\n    76\tThe matrix suite covers each runtime by store state, and the schema check validates projected entries against the history core's published JSON Schema.\n    77\t\n    78\t---\n    79\t\n    80\t## 5. RELATED\n    81\t\n    82\t- [`../README.md`](../README.md): the shared hook helpers this package sits beside.\n    83\t- [`../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md`](../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md): the lookup core and CLI that consume these readers.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"     1\t---\n     2\ttitle: \"Shared: Session Readers\"\n     3\tdescription: \"The read-only session reader package: one exact-id reader per runtime, the shared failure envelope, the capability table and the projection to the HistoryEntry list.\"\n     4\ttrigger_phrases:\n     5\t  - \"session readers\"\n     6\t  - \"read session history\"\n     7\t  - \"session reader capabilities\"\n     8\t  - \"exact session id reader\"\n     9\tversion: 1.0.0.0\n    10\t---\n    11\t\n    12\t# Shared: Session Readers\n    13\t\n    14\t---\n    15\t\n    16\t## 1. OVERVIEW\n    17\t\n    18\tThis package reads one runtime session by its exact id and returns it as the shared `HistoryEntry` list that the history lookup core takes. It never writes. A reader opens a store read-only, proves the file or row belongs to the requested session, and returns a failure code rather than a partial list.\n    19\t\n    20\tThe six decision-capture sweeps keep their own inline readers and remain the writers. Nothing here changes a save-time path.\n    21\t\n    22\t---\n    23\t\n    24\t## 2. CONTRACT\n    25\t\n    26\t- **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n    27\t- **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n    28\t- **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n    29\t- **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n    30\t\n    31\t`loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\n    32\t\n    33\t- Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n    34\t- Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\n    35\t- Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\n    36\t- DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\n    37\t\n    38\tFailure codes:\n    39\t\n    40\t| Code | Meaning |\n    41\t|---|---|\n    42\t| `locator_unavailable` | The id is empty or unsafe, or the runtime has no locator to resolve |\n    43\t| `capability_gated` | No reader exists for the runtime, or its switch is off |\n    44\t| `session_not_found` | No store record matches the id |\n    45\t| `session_mismatch` | A record was found, but its recorded id or path does not match |\n    46\t| `session_ambiguous` | More than one record claims the id |\n    47\t| `store_unreadable` | The store could not be read or projected |\n    48\t\n    49\t---\n    50\t\n    51\t## 3. FILES\n    52\t\n    53\t| File | Role |\n    54\t|---|---|\n    55\t| `index.mjs` | The dispatcher: `readSession` (projected entries), `loadSession` (raw records), the `capabilities` table and the failure envelope |\n    56\t| `identity.mjs` | Shared guards: safe session ids, path containment and the recorded-id check |\n    57\t| `project.mjs` | Projection from neutral records to `HistoryEntry`, with tool-call pairing |\n    58\t| `claude.mjs` | Claude Code transcript reader |\n    59\t| `codex.mjs` | Codex session log reader |\n    60\t| `pi.mjs` | Pi session log reader, following the live branch |\n    61\t| `opencode.mjs` | OpenCode SQLite store reader, which proves the session's recorded directory when the caller names one |\n    62\t| `devin.mjs` | Devin `sessions.db` reader over the session's main message chain and, through each compaction's `summarized_from` link, the threads before it. A recorded folder at or below the named folder passes, because Devin's hooks receive the project root. Falls back to the transcript file for a store without the session's turns |\n    63\t| `dsh.mjs` | DSH session log reader |\n    64\t| `cursor.mjs` | Cursor gate, which returns before touching any file |\n    65\t\n    66\t---\n    67\t\n    68\t## 4. VALIDATION\n    69\t\n    70\tFrom the repository root:\n    71\t\n    72\t```bash\n    73\tnode --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/\n    74\t```\n    75\t\n    76\tThe matrix suite covers each runtime by store state, and the schema check validates projected entries against the history core's published JSON Schema.\n    77\t\n    78\t---\n    79\t\n    80\t## 5. RELATED\n    81\t\n    82\t- [`../README.md`](../README.md): the shared hook helpers this package sits beside.\n    83\t- [`../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md`](../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md): the lookup core and CLI that consume these readers.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && cat -n .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551092475,"end":1794551092790}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551092817,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39492d90012yOHUwccbhO2yj","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d39476f2001foFvRVVChycgBF","type":"tool","id":"call_01974b32ebc844f1b86851db","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '365,400p' .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js; echo \"=== ENV NAMES ===\"; grep -n \"process.env\\|ENV\\b\\|_ENV =\" .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js | head -25"},"output":"function normalizeOptions(rawOptions) {\n  const options = rawOptions && typeof rawOptions === 'object' ? rawOptions : {};\n  const configuredTtl = options.cacheTTLMs ?? options.cacheTtlMs;\n  const enabled = options.enabled !== false && !envDisablesPlugin();\n  const configuredTransformDedup = typeof options.deduplicateTransforms === 'boolean'\n    ? options.deduplicateTransforms\n    : undefined;\n\n  const envCacheTTLMs = Number(process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS);\n  const envThreshold = Number(process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_THRESHOLD_CONFIDENCE);\n  const envMaxTokens = Number(process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS);\n  const envBridgeTimeoutMs = Number(process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_MS);\n  const envMaxPromptBytes = Number(process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES);\n  const envMaxBriefChars = Number(process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS);\n  const envMaxCacheEntries = Number(process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES);\n  const configuredBounding = typeof options.boundedCompiledRouteSummary === 'boolean'\n    ? options.boundedCompiledRouteSummary\n    : undefined;\n\n  return {\n    enabled,\n    cacheTTLMs: normalizePositiveInt(configuredTtl, normalizePositiveInt(envCacheTTLMs, DEFAULT_CACHE_TTL_MS)),\n    thresholdConfidence: normalizeThreshold(options.thresholdConfidence ?? (Number.isFi