{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551170850,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d395c1cf0017JiCT45TCW8jfw","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d39587fe001T8s4J62o44am92","type":"tool","id":"call_584538523a93424f8e5b179e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts | head -4; echo \"--- brief reads flag? ---\"; grep -c \"SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts; echo \"--- mutating in docs ---\"; grep -rn \"mutating\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | head -10"},"output":"103:const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000;\n119:  return parsePositiveInt(process.env.SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS);\n--- brief reads flag? ---\n0\n--- mutating in docs ---\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/ablation.md:3:description: \"Ablation harness that disables each lane in isolation and measures accuracy impact without mutating live routing weights.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/auto-indexing/sync.md:3:description: \"Write pipeline that persists derived extraction into graph-metadata.json.derived without ever mutating SKILL.md.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md:55:The three mutating commands require caller trust; an untrusted caller is\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/picomatch/README.md:281:* `returnOutput` **{Boolean}**: Implementors may use this argument to return the compiled output, instead of a regular expression. This is not exposed on the options to prevent end-users from mutating the result.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:82:- TypeScript: the `userIntent.ownedSignals` phrases become the keywords and intent signals, the command's namespace and `command` become the domains, and a `read-only` `mutating` class sets `readOnly: true`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:113:| `mutating` | `read-only`, `add-only`, `mutates` | Every metadata entry and every doctor route or action |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:124:| 3 | `mutating` is `read-only` | `run` |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:125:| 4 | `mutating` is `add-only` with `write_scope` set to `spec-folder` | `run` |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:128:`commandPolicies` in `command-bridges.generated.json` holds one record per command, or one record per route or action for a doctor command. Each record carries five keys: `command`, `route`, `mutating`, `askFirst`, `policy`. Nothing scores on it yet.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/lifecycle-routing/schema-migration.md:26:Validate that `lib/lifecycle/schema-migration.ts` performs additive backfill from the v1 schema to v2 without dropping or mutating existing fields and that a rollback to v1 leaves original data intact.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"103:const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000;\n119:  return parsePositiveInt(process.env.SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS);\n--- brief reads flag? ---\n0\n--- mutating in docs ---\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/ablation.md:3:description: \"Ablation harness that disables each lane in isolation and measures accuracy impact without mutating live routing weights.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/auto-indexing/sync.md:3:description: \"Write pipeline that persists derived extraction into graph-metadata.json.derived without ever mutating SKILL.md.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md:55:The three mutating commands require caller trust; an untrusted caller is\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/picomatch/README.md:281:* `returnOutput` **{Boolean}**: Implementors may use this argument to return the compiled output, instead of a regular expression. This is not exposed on the options to prevent end-users from mutating the result.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:82:- TypeScript: the `userIntent.ownedSignals` phrases become the keywords and intent signals, the command's namespace and `command` become the domains, and a `read-only` `mutating` class sets `readOnly: true`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:113:| `mutating` | `read-only`, `add-only`, `mutates` | Every metadata entry and every doctor route or action |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:124:| 3 | `mutating` is `read-only` | `run` |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:125:| 4 | `mutating` is `add-only` with `write_scope` set to `spec-folder` | `run` |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:128:`commandPolicies` in `command-bridges.generated.json` holds one record per command, or one record per route or action for a doctor command. Each record carries five keys: `command`, `route`, `mutating`, `askFirst`, `policy`. Nothing scores on it yet.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/lifecycle-routing/schema-migration.md:26:Validate that `lib/lifecycle/schema-migration.ts` performs additive backfill from the v1 schema to v2 without dropping or mutating existing fields and that a rollback to v1 leaves original data intact.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"ra