{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551690153,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39d014e002U0GfNS2J43B1Tt","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d39ce681001Hn7kODTHxWwhAg","type":"tool","id":"call_8c8dbaa070de47be8befa797","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Report — `render-hooks-plugin` lineage\n\nRun: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-1794550137809-1ecgc7` · generation 1 · lineage mode `new`\nTarget: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\nArtifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin`\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- Overall verdict: **PASS** with advisories\n- hasAdvisories: **true**\n- Findings: **0 P0, 0 P1, 11 P2** active; 2 closed by adjudication\n- Iterations: 5 of 5 (`maxIterations` reached, not converged by threshold)\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4 of 4)\n- Review scope: the 53 `render-hooks-plugin` rows of `review/review-scope.txt` — the OpenCode advisor plugin, the shared session-reader package, the advisor runtime render/spawn/CLI surfaces, the runtime-mirror sync scripts, the spec-gate core, and the shared `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 section.\n- Operator review focus: Code review of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope.txt lists the changed files, one per line as area TAB path. Review the files whose area equals your lineage label (last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir), plus shared docs that describe them. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line. Check: behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows; docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text (split holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, or holdout-prompts.jsonl): counts only. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n\nWhat the operator asked, and what this pass found:\n\n- **Behaviour on the six named runtimes** — one dispatcher, four changed readers, and a capability table that names all six plus `cursor`. No P0/P1. The defects are in the edges: a link opened after being checked under its resolved path, a DSH event without a `source` losing the operator turn, and a corrupt Devin database shadowing a readable transcript.\n- **Safety of offering a mutating command** — the guard is sound where it runs: `start`, `ask` and every non-read-only `run` render as `(parent-named only)` for a child. Two gaps remain advisory: the trigger is a process-wide environment marker with no per-session override, and the downgrade reads mutability from the skill row rather than from the command actually printed.\n- **Holdout hygiene** — clean. No file in this area opens a holdout store; the only textual match is a validation note. No holdout row was read or printed.\n- **Docs that disagree with code** — two real drifts: a document naming a timeout consumer that never reads the variable, and an offer contract that omits the field which gates a child.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for the verdict. Eleven advisory P2 findings are recorded for a follow-up pass; none blocks release.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Planning Packet\": {\n    \"triggered\": false,\n    \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n    \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n    \"activeFindings\": [\n      {\"id\": \"R1-P2-002\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R1-P2-003\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R1-P2-004\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R1-P2-005\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R2-P2-002\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"security\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R2-P2-003\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"security\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R3-P2-001\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"traceability\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R3-P2-002\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"traceability\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R4-P2-001\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"maintainability\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R4-P2-002\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"maintainability\"},\n      {\"id\": \"R4-P2-003\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"dimension\": \"maintainability\"}\n    ],\n    \"remediationWorkstreams\": [],\n    \"specSeed\": [\n      \"Record the session-reader identity rule: the path that is checked is the path that is opened.\",\n      \"Record that the child-session command downgrade is keyed on AI_SESSION_CHILD and has no per-session override.\",\n      \"Record that a command row's mutating class is the only input to the child downgrade.\"\n    ],\n    \"planSeed\": [],\n    \"findingClasses\": [\"cross-consumer\", \"class-of-bug\", \"instance-only\"],\n    \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n      \"session-reader dispatcher\",\n      \"claude/devine/dsh readers\",\n      \"brief renderer\",\n      \"advisor subprocess\",\n      \"feature catalog\",\n      \"root AGENTS.md Gate 2\"\n    ],\n    \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false,\n    \"note\": \"Advisory only. No remediation workstream is opened because no active P0 or P1 exists; the eleven P2 items are recorded for a separate hardening pass.\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n### R1-P2-002 — Containment is proven on the resolved path while the bytes are opened from the caller's path\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: correctness · Finding class: cross-consumer\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:213`, opened at `:217`; same split at `devin.mjs:350`/`:354` and `dsh.mjs:306`/`:310`\n- Evidence: `storePath = containment.path` records the checked path; `readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8')` opens the caller's path. `pi.mjs:246-256` closes the same gap by reading the guard's resolved path.\n- Impact: `source.storePath` can name a file other than the one whose bytes produced the records.\n- Fix: read `containment.path` in all three readers, matching `pi.mjs`.\n- Disposition: open · Scope proof: `rg -n \"storePath = containment.path\"` returns exactly the three readers\n\n### R1-P2-003 — A DSH operator message with no `source` object is silently reclassified as injected\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: correctness · Finding class: instance-only\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195`, classification at `:250-253`\n- Evidence: a record requires `data.source?.kind === 'user'`; every other `user/message` becomes an `injected` entry with source `unknown`.\n- Impact: an operator turn disappears from history while the read still reports `ok: true`.\n- Fix: treat a missing `source` object as operator content, or reject the event, and pin the case in `injected-text.test.mjs`.\n- Disposition: open (narrowed: `session-readers/README.md:36` shows the absent case was considered)\n\n### R1-P2-004 — A corrupt Devin `sessions.db` suppresses the transcript fallback\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: correctness · Finding class: class-of-bug\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:395`, `:403`, `:439`, fall-through at `:447`\n- Evidence: only an absent row or an empty projection reaches `loadTranscript`; an open or projection failure returns `store_unreadable`.\n- Impact: a truncated or locked database hides a readable `transcripts/<sessionId>.json` on the same machine.\n- Fix: fall through to the transcript on a database read failure, keeping the database error as a diagnostic.\n- Disposition: open\n\n### R1-P2-005 — `needsMode` withholding is defeated when the skill also has a generated command row\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: correctness · Finding class: instance-only\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:226`, `:549-552`\n- Evidence: `recommendation.command ?? row?.command` backfills a withheld command; the `(needs a mode)` head applies only when no row exists.\n- Impact: a prompt that names no single mode can still be answered with one runnable command.\n- Fix: when `needsMode` is set, never backfill from the row.\n- Disposition: open (narrowed: `skill-advisor-hook.md:53` documents the general precedence)\n\n### R2-P2-002 — The low-level advisor spawn accumulates child output without a byte cap\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: security · Finding class: cross-consumer\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:239`\n- Evidence: `stdout += chunk` has no ceiling; the fallback path caps the same stream at `MAX_STDOUT_BYTES` (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:214-219`).\n- Impact: a CLI that keeps writing grows the caller's heap for the whole timeout.\n- Fix: apply the same `capStdout` bound in `runSpawnAttempt`.\n- Disposition: open\n\n### R2-P2-003 — The child downgrade reads mutability from the skill row, not from the command that is printed\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: security · Finding class: instance-only\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:233`\n- Evidence: `policyWord(policy, row?.mutating, childSession)` while the printed command may come from `recommendation.command` (`:226`).\n- Impact: a caller-supplied command can be judged by another command's mutability class.\n- Fix: resolve `mutating` for the command that is actually printed.\n- Disposition: open\n\n### R3-P2-001 — A documented timeout consumer never reads the timeout variable\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: traceability · Finding class: instance-only\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:176`\n- Evidence: the line names `skill-advisor-brief.ts`; that file contains no occurrence of `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS`. `subprocess.ts:119` does read it, against `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000`.\n- Impact: a maintainer looks for the flag's effect in a file that has none.\n- Fix: drop the file from the consumer list, or make it read the flag.\n- Disposition: open\n\n### R3-P2-002 — The documented recommendation contract omits the field that decides the child-session downgrade\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: traceability · Finding class: class-of-bug\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:41`\n- Evidence: the contract names four fields; `command-attach.ts:51` carries a fifth, `mutating`, and `render.ts:233` is its only reader.\n- Impact: the guard's single input is absent from the contract that describes the offer.\n- Fix: add `mutating` and its vocabulary to the contract section.\n- Disposition: open\n\n### R4-P2-001 — A fourth hand-spelled runtime list sits outside the parity test that exists to catch exactly this\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: maintainability · Finding class: class-of-bug\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:28`\n- Evidence: seven runtimes spelled by hand, the same seven as `advisor-runtime-values.ts:10-18`; `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` ties three lists and not this one.\n- Impact: a runtime added to the tuple passes every parity test and stays gated in `readSession`.\n- Fix: derive `capabilities` from the tuple, or add it to the parity comparison.\n- Disposition: open\n\n### R4-P2-002 — The child-session marker is interpreted twice, once through an exported constant and once as a hard-coded literal\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: maintainability · Finding class: cross-consumer\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs:101`\n- Evidence: `CHILD_SESSION_ENV` and `isChildSession(env)` exist in the spec-gate core; `render.ts:522` writes the literal inline. Both accept `'1'` today.\n- Impact: a change to the accepted value updates one reader and silently skips the other.\n- Fix: have the renderer import the shared helper.\n- Disposition: open\n\n### R4-P2-003 — The operator-facing direct-call example puts the prompt in argv, against the guarantee the hook path keeps\n\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: maintainability · Finding class: instance-only\n- File: `AGENTS.md:65`\n- Evidence: the Gate 2 example passes the prompt as an argv JSON string; `skill-advisor-hook.md:38` states the stdin guarantee the same section points to.\n- Impact: the diagnostic path exposes the prompt in the process table.\n- Fix: show the stdin form in the Gate 2 example.\n- Disposition: open\n\n### Closed by adjudication\n\n- **R1-P2-001** — resolved. `session-readers/README.md:42-43` specifies that an empty or unsafe id yields `locator_unavailable` before the runtime resolves, which is what `index.mjs:99-102` does. Documented contract, not a defect.\n- **R2-P1-001** — resolved at P1. `render.ts:522` keys the child downgrade on `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, and `skill-advisor-hook.md:39` documents that exact trigger. Code and document agree; the residual is carried as a Deferred Item.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\nNo workstream is opened. The verdict is PASS with advisories and no active P0 or P1 exists.\n\nFor the follow-up hardening pass, the suggested order is by blast radius:\n\n1. **Reader path identity** — R1-P2-002 (three files, one mechanical change).\n2. **Reader data loss** — R1-P2-003, R1-P2-004 (two readers, each with a test to add).\n3. **Advisor resource bound** — R2-P2-002 (one function, mirrors an existing helper).\n4. **Offer-contract clarity** — R1-P2-005, R2-P2-003, R3-P2-002 (one renderer plus two documents).\n5. **Vocabulary ownership** — R4-P2-001, R4-P2-002 (two modules, one test).\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- State, in the session-reader contract, that the path proven by containment is the path opened.\n- State, in the child-session rule, that `AI_SESSION_CHILD` is a process marker and that no per-session override exists today.\n- State, in the recommendation contract, that a command row's `mutating` class is the only input to the child downgrade.\n- State, in the capability table section, that the advisor runtime tuple is the canonical list and every other runtime list derives from it.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Read `containment.path` instead of the caller's path in `claude.mjs`, `devin.mjs` and `dsh.mjs`.\n- Add the absent-`source` DSH case to `injected-text.test.mjs` before changing `dsh.mjs:195`.\n- Cap `runSpawnAttempt`'s stdout and stderr with the existing `capStdout` helper.\n- Resolve `mutating` for the printed command in `commandLabel`.\n- Add `mutating` to `advisor-recommend.md`'s contract section.\n- Point the renderer at `CHILD_SESSION_ENV` / `isChildSession`.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Unresolved drift |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | pass | Every documented claim checked in iterations 3 and 5 has a matching code path except the consumer list in R3-P2-001 | R3-P2-001, R3-P2-002 |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No checklist rows exist for this area; the review is of changed code, not packet acceptance criteria | none |\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Unresolved drift |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `skill_agent` | partial | `skill-advisor-hook.md:88` names the Claude shim chain; the source half resolves, the dist half was not read | coverage gap, not a finding |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | Six adapters plus one plugin; seven runtimes in the tuple and the same seven in the capability table | R4-P2-001 |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | Compiled-route options, one-command-per-label, and the typed-command degraded entry all confirmed | R3-P2-002 |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No manual-testing playbook row covers this area | none |\n\n`AC_COVERAGE`: exempt — the review target is a spec-folder parent, and this lineage reviewed changed implementation files rather than the packet's acceptance criteria.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- **Child-session guard per-session override.** The downgrade input is the documented process marker. A host that dispatches a child in-process without setting `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` would receive a fully visible mutating command. No such host was demonstrated, so this is hardening, not a finding. Reopens as P1 if one is shown.\n- **Unread modules.** `spec-gate-core.mjs` beyond `:71-310` (1888 lines total), `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` internals (465 lines), `embedders/schema.ts` internals (377 lines), eight runtime test suites, and the Claude dist half of the hook chain. These are read-scope limits, not clean surfaces.\n- **`.d.mts` declaration files.** Not reviewed as behaviour; they carry types only.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Saturated directions: declaration-file signature parity (iteration 1), plugin-README runtime matrix (iteration 2).\n- Completed pivots: 1 → 2 (correctness → security), 2 → 3 (security → traceability), 3 → 4 (traceability → maintainability), 4 → 5 (maintainability → adjudication).\n- Failed pivots: 0.\n- Audited overrides: 0.\n- Council artifact references: none (single-lineage review, no Council pass).\n- Selected review directions: reader identity and data loss; command-offer safety; documentation-to-code drift; vocabulary ownership.\n- Remaining frontier: the unread modules and the Claude dist chain listed under Deferred Items.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n- Covered bug classes: contract violation, silent data loss, error-path masking, privileged command offer, prompt injection, holdout leakage, documentation drift, contract omission, duplicated vocabulary, missing test coverage.\n- Ruled out: path traversal in `claude.mjs`, chain-cycle truncation in `devin.mjs`, prompt text in argv, a relabelable `mutating` class, holdout reads (twice), a duplicated brief renderer, `spec-gate-core` render duplication, a dead documented timeout variable, a self-starting offered command.\n- Deferred: `spec-gate-core.mjs` internals, `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` internals, `embedders/schema.ts` internals, eight runtime test suites, the Claude dist chain.\n- Blocked: none.\n- Graph coverage mode: `graphless_fallback` (no graph was available; every search was a direct read or an exact search).\n- Search debt: none recorded by the reducer.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence\n\n| Iteration | Focus | New findings | Ratio | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | correctness | 5 P2 | 1.00 | PASS |\n| 2 | security | 1 P1, 2 P2 | 1.00 | CONDITIONAL |\n| 3 | traceability | 2 P2 (1 P1 closed, 1 P2 closed) | 0.33 | PASS |\n| 4 | maintainability | 3 P2 | 0.23 | PASS |\n| 5 | adjudication | 0 new (2 closed) | 0.15 | PASS |\n\nStop reason: `maxIterationsReached`. The threshold of 0.10 was not met on the final ratio of 0.15, and the iteration ceiling of 5 was reached. Release readiness: `in-progress`.\n\n### Coverage\n\n- Dimensions: 4 of 4 (`dimensionCoverage` all true in the registry).\n- Files: 30 of 53 scope files read in full or in the substantive part; the gaps are listed under Deferred Items.\n- Integration surfaces named: `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/*`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/*`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/*`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`, `AGENTS.md`.\n\n### Sources reviewed\n\n- Iteration files: `iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iterations/iteration-005.md`\n- Deltas: `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` … `deltas/iter-005.jsonl`\n- Registry, strategy and dashboard as refreshed by the reducer after each iteration.\n\n### Rule sources\n\n`Rule sources: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md. Overrides: none. Refused: none. Ignored: none. Conflicts: none`\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Report — `render-hooks-plugin` lineage\\n\\nRun: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-1794550137809-1ecgc7` · generation 1 · lineage mode `new`\\nTarget: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\nArtifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin`\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- Overall verdict: **PASS** with advisories\\n- hasAdvisories: **true**\\n- Findings: **0 P0, 0 P1, 11 P2** active; 2 closed by adjudication\\n- Iterations: 5 of 5 (`maxIterations` reached, not converged by threshold)\\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4 of 4)\\n- Review scope: the 53 `render-hooks-plugin` rows of `review/review-scope.txt` — the OpenCode advisor plugin, the shared session-reader package, the advisor runtime render/spawn/CLI surfaces, the runtime-mirror sync scripts, the spec-gate core, and the shared `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 section.\\n- Operator review focus: Code review of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope.txt lists the changed files, one per line as area TAB path. Review the files whose area equals your lineage label (last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir), plus shared docs that describe them. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line. Check: behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows; docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text (split holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, or holdout-prompts.jsonl): counts only. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\\n\\nWhat the operator asked, and what this pass found:\\n\\n- **Behaviour on the six named runtimes** — one dispatcher, four changed readers, and a capability table that names all six plus `cursor`. No P0/P1. The defects are in the edges: a link opened after being checked under its resolved path, a DSH event without a `source` losing the operator turn, and a corrupt Devin database shadowing a readable transcript.\\n- **Safety of offering a mutating command** — the guard is sound where it runs: `start`, `ask` and every non-read-only `run` render as `(parent-named only)` for a child. Two gaps remain advisory: the trigger is a process-wide environment marker with no per-session override, and the downgrade reads mutability from the skill row rather than from the command actually printed.\\n- **Holdout hygiene** — clean. No file in this area opens a holdout store; the only textual match is a validation note. No holdout row was read or printed.\\n- **Docs that disagree with code** — two real drifts: a document naming a timeout consumer that never reads the variable, and an offer contract that omits the field which gates a child.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for the verdict. Eleven advisory P2 findings are recorded for a follow-up pass; none blocks release.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"Planning Packet\\\": {\\n    \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n    \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n    \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n    \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-P2-002\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-P2-003\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-P2-004\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-P2-005\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R2-P2-002\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"security\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R2-P2-003\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"security\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-P2-001\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"traceability\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-P2-002\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"traceability\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-P2-001\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"maintainability\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-P2-002\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"maintainability\\\"},\\n      {\\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-P2-003\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"maintainability\\\"}\\n    ],\\n    \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [],\\n    \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n      \\\"Record the session-reader identity rule: the path that is checked is the path that is opened.\\\",\\n      \\\"Record that the child-session command downgrade is keyed on AI_SESSION_CHILD and has no per-session override.\\\",\\n      \\\"Record that a command row's mutating class is the only input to the child downgrade.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"planSeed\\\": [],\\n    \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"cross-consumer\\\", \\\"class-of-bug\\\", \\\"instance-only\\\"],\\n    \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n      \\\"session-reader dispatcher\\\",\\n      \\\"claude/devine/dsh readers\\\",\\n      \\\"brief renderer\\\",\\n      \\\"advisor subprocess\\\",\\n      \\\"feature catalog\\\",\\n      \\\"root AGENTS.md Gate 2\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false,\\n    \\\"note\\\": \\\"Advisory only. No remediation workstream is opened because no active P0 or P1 exists; the eleven P2 items are recorded for a separate hardening pass.\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n### R1-P2-002 — Containment is proven on the resolved path while the bytes are opened from the caller's path\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: correctness · Finding class: cross-consumer\\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:213`, opened at `:217`; same split at `devin.mjs:350`/`:354` and `dsh.mjs:306`/`:310`\\n- Evidence: `storePath = containment.path` records the checked path; `readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8')` opens the caller's path. `pi.mjs:246-256` closes the same gap by reading the guard's resolved path.\\n- Impact: `source.storePath` can name a file other than the one whose bytes produced the records.\\n- Fix: read `containment.path` in all three readers, matching `pi.mjs`.\\n- Disposition: open · Scope proof: `rg -n \\\"storePath = containment.path\\\"` returns exactly the three readers\\n\\n### R1-P2-003 — A DSH operator message with no `source` object is silently reclassified as injected\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: correctness · Finding class: instance-only\\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195`, classification at `:250-253`\\n- Evidence: a record requires `data.source?.kind === 'user'`; every other `user/message` becomes an `injected` entry with source `unknown`.\\n- Impact: an operator turn disappears from history while the read still reports `ok: true`.\\n- Fix: treat a missing `source` object as operator content, or reject the event, and pin the case in `injected-text.test.mjs`.\\n- Disposition: open (narrowed: `session-readers/README.md:36` shows the absent case was considered)\\n\\n### R1-P2-004 — A corrupt Devin `sessions.db` suppresses the transcript fallback\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: correctness · Finding class: class-of-bug\\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:395`, `:403`, `:439`, fall-through at `:447`\\n- Evidence: only an absent row or an empty projection reaches `loadTranscript`; an open or projection failure returns `store_unreadable`.\\n- Impact: a truncated or locked database hides a readable `transcripts/<sessionId>.json` on the same machine.\\n- Fix: fall through to the transcript on a database read failure, keeping the database error as a diagnostic.\\n- Disposition: open\\n\\n### R1-P2-005 — `needsMode` withholding is defeated when the skill also has a generated command row\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: correctness · Finding class: instance-only\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:226`, `:549-552`\\n- Evidence: `recommendation.command ?? row?.command` backfills a withheld command; the `(needs a mode)` head applies only when no row exists.\\n- Impact: a prompt that names no single mode can still be answered with one runnable command.\\n- Fix: when `needsMode` is set, never backfill from the row.\\n- Disposition: open (narrowed: `skill-advisor-hook.md:53` documents the general precedence)\\n\\n### R2-P2-002 — The low-level advisor spawn accumulates child output without a byte cap\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: security · Finding class: cross-consumer\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:239`\\n- Evidence: `stdout += chunk` has no ceiling; the fallback path caps the same stream at `MAX_STDOUT_BYTES` (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:214-219`).\\n- Impact: a CLI that keeps writing grows the caller's heap for the whole timeout.\\n- Fix: apply the same `capStdout` bound in `runSpawnAttempt`.\\n- Disposition: open\\n\\n### R2-P2-003 — The child downgrade reads mutability from the skill row, not from the command that is printed\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: security · Finding class: instance-only\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:233`\\n- Evidence: `policyWord(policy, row?.mutating, childSession)` while the printed command may come from `recommendation.command` (`:226`).\\n- Impact: a caller-supplied command can be judged by another command's mutability class.\\n- Fix: resolve `mutating` for the command that is actually printed.\\n- Disposition: open\\n\\n### R3-P2-001 — A documented timeout consumer never reads the timeout variable\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: traceability · Finding class: instance-only\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:176`\\n- Evidence: the line names `skill-advisor-brief.ts`; that file contains no occurrence of `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS`. `subprocess.ts:119` does read it, against `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000`.\\n- Impact: a maintainer looks for the flag's effect in a file that has none.\\n- Fix: drop the file from the consumer list, or make it read the flag.\\n- Disposition: open\\n\\n### R3-P2-002 — The documented recommendation contract omits the field that decides the child-session downgrade\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: traceability · Finding class: class-of-bug\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:41`\\n- Evidence: the contract names four fields; `command-attach.ts:51` carries a fifth, `mutating`, and `render.ts:233` is its only reader.\\n- Impact: the guard's single input is absent from the contract that describes the offer.\\n- Fix: add `mutating` and its vocabulary to the contract section.\\n- Disposition: open\\n\\n### R4-P2-001 — A fourth hand-spelled runtime list sits outside the parity test that exists to catch exactly this\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: maintainability · Finding class: class-of-bug\\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:28`\\n- Evidence: seven runtimes spelled by hand, the same seven as `advisor-runtime-values.ts:10-18`; `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` ties three lists and not this one.\\n- Impact: a runtime added to the tuple passes every parity test and stays gated in `readSession`.\\n- Fix: derive `capabilities` from the tuple, or add it to the parity comparison.\\n- Disposition: open\\n\\n### R4-P2-002 — The child-session marker is interpreted twice, once through an exported constant and once as a hard-coded literal\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: maintainability · Finding class: cross-consumer\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs:101`\\n- Evidence: `CHILD_SESSION_ENV` and `isChildSession(env)` exist in the spec-gate core; `render.ts:522` writes the literal inline. Both accept `'1'` today.\\n- Impact: a change to the accepted value updates one reader and silently skips the other.\\n- Fix: have the renderer import the shared helper.\\n- Disposition: open\\n\\n### R4-P2-003 — The operator-facing direct-call example puts the prompt in argv, against the guarantee the hook path keeps\\n\\n- Severity: P2 · Dimension: maintainability · Finding class: instance-only\\n- File: `AGENTS.md:65`\\n- Evidence: the Gate 2 example passes the prompt as an argv JSON string; `skill-advisor-hook.md:38` states the stdin guarantee the same section points to.\\n- Impact: the diagnostic path exposes the prompt in the process table.\\n- Fix: show the stdin form in the Gate 2 example.\\n- Disposition: open\\n\\n### Closed by adjudication\\n\\n- **R1-P2-001** — resolved. `session-readers/README.md:42-43` specifies that an empty or unsafe id yields `locator_unavailable` before the runtime resolves, which is what `index.mjs:99-102` does. Documented contract, not a defect.\\n- **R2-P1-001** — resolved at P1. `render.ts:522` keys the child downgrade on `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, and `skill-advisor-hook.md:39` documents that exact trigger. Code and document agree; the residual is carried as a Deferred Item.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\nNo workstream is opened. The verdict is PASS with advisories and no active P0 or P1 exists.\\n\\nFor the follow-up hardening pass, the suggested order is by blast radius:\\n\\n1. **Reader path identity** — R1-P2-002 (three files, one mechanical change).\\n2. **Reader data loss** — R1-P2-003, R1-P2-004 (two readers, each with a test to add).\\n3. **Advisor resource bound** — R2-P2-002 (one function, mirrors an existing helper).\\n4. **Offer-contract clarity** — R1-P2-005, R2-P2-003, R3-P2-002 (one renderer plus two documents).\\n5. **Vocabulary ownership** — R4-P2-001, R4-P2-002 (two modules, one test).\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- State, in the session-reader contract, that the path proven by containment is the path opened.\\n- State, in the child-session rule, that `AI_SESSION_CHILD` is a process marker and that no per-session override exists today.\\n- State, in the recommendation contract, that a command row's `mutating` class is the only input to the child downgrade.\\n- State, in the capability table section, that the advisor runtime tuple is the canonical list and every other runtime list derives from it.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Read `containment.path` instead of the caller's path in `claude.mjs`, `devin.mjs` and `dsh.mjs`.\\n- Add the absent-`source` DSH case to `injected-text.test.mjs` before changing `dsh.mjs:195`.\\n- Cap `runSpawnAttempt`'s stdout and stderr with the existing `capStdout` helper.\\n- Resolve `mutating` for the printed command in `commandLabel`.\\n- Add `mutating` to `advisor-recommend.md`'s contract section.\\n- Point the renderer at `CHILD_SESSION_ENV` / `isChildSession`.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Unresolved drift |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | Every documented claim checked in iterations 3 and 5 has a matching code path except the consumer list in R3-P2-001 | R3-P2-001, R3-P2-002 |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No checklist rows exist for this area; the review is of changed code, not packet acceptance criteria | none |\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Unresolved drift |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `skill_agent` | partial | `skill-advisor-hook.md:88` names the Claude shim chain; the source half resolves, the dist half was not read | coverage gap, not a finding |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | Six adapters plus one plugin; seven runtimes in the tuple and the same seven in the capability table | R4-P2-001 |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | Compiled-route options, one-command-per-label, and the typed-command degraded entry all confirmed | R3-P2-002 |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No manual-testing playbook row covers this area | none |\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE`: exempt — the review target is a spec-folder parent, and this lineage reviewed changed implementation files rather than the packet's acceptance criteria.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- **Child-session guard per-session override.** The downgrade input is the documented process marker. A host that dispatches a child in-process without setting `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` would receive a fully visible mutating command. No such host was demonstrated, so this is hardening, not a finding. Reopens as P1 if one is shown.\\n- **Unread modules.** `spec-gate-core.mjs` beyond `:71-310` (1888 lines total), `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` internals (465 lines), `embedders/schema.ts` internals (377 lines), eight runtime test suites, and the Claude dist half of the hook chain. These are read-scope limits, not clean surfaces.\\n- **`.d.mts` declaration files.** Not reviewed as behaviour; they carry types only.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Saturated directions: declaration-file signature parity (iteration 1), plugin-README runtime matrix (iteration 2).\\n- Completed pivots: 1 → 2 (correctness → security), 2 → 3 (security → traceability), 3 → 4 (traceability → maintainability), 4 → 5 (maintainability → adjudication).\\n- Failed pivots: 0.\\n- Audited overrides: 0.\\n- Council artifact references: none (single-lineage review, no Council pass).\\n- Selected review directions: reader identity and data loss; command-offer safety; documentation-to-code drift; vocabulary ownership.\\n- Remaining frontier: the unread modules and the Claude dist chain listed under Deferred Items.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n- Covered bug classes: contract violation, silent data loss, error-path masking, privileged command offer, prompt injection, holdout leakage, documentation drift, contract omission, duplicated vocabulary, missing test coverage.\\n- Ruled out: path traversal in `claude.mjs`, chain-cycle truncation in `devin.mjs`, prompt text in argv, a relabelable `mutating` class, holdout reads (twice), a duplicated brief renderer, `spec-gate-core` render duplication, a dead documented timeout variable, a self-starting offered command.\\n- Deferred: `spec-gate-core.mjs` internals, `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` internals, `embedders/schema.ts` internals, eight runtime test suites, the Claude dist chain.\\n- Blocked: none.\\n- Graph coverage mode: `graphless_fallback` (no graph was available; every search was a direct read or an exact search).\\n- Search debt: none recorded by the reducer.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence\\n\\n| Iteration | Focus | New findings | Ratio | Verdict |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | correctness | 5 P2 | 1.00 | PASS |\\n| 2 | security | 1 P1, 2 P2 | 1.00 | CONDITIONAL |\\n| 3 | traceability | 2 P2 (1 P1 closed, 1 P2 closed) | 0.33 | PASS |\\n| 4 | maintainability | 3 P2 | 0.23 | PASS |\\n| 5 | adjudication | 0 new (2 closed) | 0.15 | PASS |\\n\\nStop reason: `maxIterationsReached`. The threshold of 0.10 was not met on the final ratio of 0.15, and the iteration ceiling of 5 was reached. Release readiness: `in-progress`.\\n\\n### Coverage\\n\\n- Dimensions: 4 of 4 (`dimensionCoverage` all true in the registry).\\n- Files: 30 of 53 scope files read in full or in the substantive part; the gaps are listed under Deferred Items.\\n- Integration surfaces named: `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/*`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/*`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/*`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`, `AGENTS.md`.\\n\\n### Sources reviewed\\n\\n- Iteration files: `iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iterations/iteration-005.md`\\n- Deltas: `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` … `deltas/iter-005.jsonl`\\n- Registry, strategy and dashboard as refreshed by the reducer after each iteration.\\n\\n### Rule sources\\n\\n`Rule sources: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md. Overrides: none. Refused: none. Ignored: none. Conflicts: none`\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551644494,"end":1794551690153}}}}
