{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551760554,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39eb0520018AtUd5mlau6f1u","sessionID":"ses_e2c799690ffeJQrMJ5OzboPGaV","messageID":"msg_1d39e60d1001pT8GHAyvxgUaau","type":"tool","id":"call_896785505bcd4533881ca77a","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading each session reader against its own test file surfaced contract drift faster than reading the reader alone (iteration 1).\n- Following the hook path from the plugin into `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` found the degraded-mode contract in one pass (iteration 1).\n- Mapping the operator's six runtime names onto four concrete reader files and one dispatcher prevented a generic cross-runtime finding (iteration 2).\n- Pairing every document claim with the code it names, one row per claim, turned an open-ended \"do the docs match\" question into a finite table (iteration 3).\n- Comparing the runtime tuple with every other list of runtime names found the one copy no test covers (iteration 4).\n- Re-reading each active finding's cited line before closing it caught two entries that documentary evidence no longer supported (iteration 5).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Treating `.d.mts` declaration files as independent evidence produced only \"consistent by construction\" results (iteration 1).\n- Assuming the plugin README describes runtime coverage; it documents hooks, not per-runtime readers (iteration 2).\n- Reading `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` as a dead knob: it is live in `subprocess.ts:119`, and the README line was about the hub rather than the plugin (iteration 3)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -69,15 +69,22 @@\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading each session reader against its own test file surfaced contract drift faster than reading the reader alone (iteration 1).\n+- Following the hook path from the plugin into `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` found the degraded-mode contract in one pass (iteration 1).\n+- Mapping the operator's six runtime names onto four concrete reader files and one dispatcher prevented a generic cross-runtime finding (iteration 2).\n+- Pairing every document claim with the code it names, one row per claim, turned an open-ended \"do the docs match\" question into a finite table (iteration 3).\n+- Comparing the runtime tuple with every other list of runtime names found the one copy no test covers (iteration 4).\n+- Re-reading each active finding's cited line before closing it caught two entries that documentary evidence no longer supported (iteration 5).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Treating `.d.mts` declaration files as independent evidence produced only \"consistent by construction\" results (iteration 1).\n+- Assuming the plugin README describes runtime coverage; it documents hooks, not per-runtime readers (iteration 2).\n+- Reading `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` as a dead knob: it is live in `subprocess.ts:119`, and the README line was about the hub rather than the plugin (iteration 3).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":9,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading each session reader against its own test file surfaced contract drift faster than reading the reader alone (iteration 1).\\n- Following the hook path from the plugin into `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` found the degraded-mode contract in one pass (iteration 1).\\n- Mapping the operator's six runtime names onto four concrete reader files and one dispatcher prevented a generic cross-runtime finding (iteration 2).\\n- Pairing every document claim with the code it names, one row per claim, turned an open-ended \\\"do the docs match\\\" question into a finite table (iteration 3).\\n- Comparing the runtime tuple with every other list of runtime names found the one copy no test covers (iteration 4).\\n- Re-reading each active finding's cited line before closing it caught two entries that documentary evidence no longer supported (iteration 5).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Treating `.d.mts` declaration files as independent evidence produced only \\\"consistent by construction\\\" results (iteration 1).\\n- Assuming the plugin README describes runtime coverage; it documents hooks, not per-runtime readers (iteration 2).\\n- Reading `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` as a dead knob: it is live in `subprocess.ts:119`, and the README line was about the hub rather than the plugin (iteration 3).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551754834,"end":1794551760554}}}}
